\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dollar at 2-1/2 yr high; Indian rupee hits 20-mnth peak\b0\par\par\uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2017\par 07:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Anusha Ravindranath\par     April 26 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par stronger on Wednesday with the Taiwan dollar at a two-and-a-half\par year high, spurred by persistent foreign inflows, while the\par Indian rupee climbed to a 20-month peak, buoyed by a local stock\par market rally.\par     The Taiwan dollar rose for a fifth day and was at\par its strongest level against the U.S. dollar since September\par 2014. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tracked the strength in local equities, which\par rose mirroring an overnight rally on Wall Street and as retail\par investors joined the foreign buying spree.\par \par     The Indian rupee gained for a third straight\par session and took cues from the record rally in local share\par market after a host of strong domestic quarterly results and\par hopes for additional foreign inflows to India boosted sentiment.\par     "Even as there are likely gains in the dollar, on the\par domestic front, excess rupee liquidity in the banking sector and\par continuous (foreign inflows) could prevent the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market," \f28 \uc2 \f2 HDFC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par said in a note.\par     "Therefore, the rupee could continue to trade with an\par appreciation bias in the near-term." \par     Meanwhile, investors in broader Asia shifted their focus to\par a major tax announcement by U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 . He is\par set to unveil a tax plan on Wednesday, with markets anticipating\par a sharp slash in corporate income tax rates.\par     Trump's proposal to exclude the controversial\par "border-adjustment" tax on imports will come as a relief for\par export oriented countries such as Taiwan and South Korea.\par     "If the tax reforms come as expected, it is going to be\par supportive for Asian equities and we can expect a bit more\par appreciation in the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  going forward, just from\par the lift in risk appetite," Chang Wei Liang an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\par     The dollar surged against the safe-haven yen on Tuesday as \par strong new U.S. home sales data and optimism surrounding the\par expected tax reforms soothed sentiment.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announces the outcome of its\par monetary policy meeting on Thursday and is expected to keep its\par policy settings steady.\par     \par     MALAYSIAN RINGGIT \par     The ringgit rose for a second day to a five-month\par peak.\par     Mizuho's Chang said the ringgit is benefiting from the\par recently announced liberalisation of its onshore markets, which\par helps address foreign investor concerns about managing their\par risk exposure in that market. \par     "We believe that (announcement) could potentially revive\par inflows into Malaysia," he said.\par     Recently, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara\f28 \uc2 \f2  unveiled plans to ease the hedging\par rules in the onshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) and bond markets\par in Malaysia. (\f28 {