\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fragile Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  set for weekly losses on rising dollar, US yields\b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2016\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds text, updates prices)\par     * Rupee up as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank's heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted\par     * Yuan gains after China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected on Thursday\par     * Ringgit, rupiah lead weekly emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 25 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par saw marginal gains on Friday but   looked set for weekly losses\par as the stronger dollar and higher \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields prompt\par global investors to dump regional assets.\par     The Indian rupee led daily gains as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in morning trade when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par to around 68.65 per dollar, approaching the record low hit in\par the previous session, traders said. \par     China's yuan edged up from 8-1/2-year lows hit on\par Thursday as some investors and companies sold dollars to take\par profits amid caution that state-owned banks could provide dollar\par liquidity near the 6.92 level to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The yuan's rebound prompted traders to cut some of their\par bearish bets on the South Korean won and the\par Singapore dollar.\par     Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also got a breather on Friday as the\par U.S. dollar stepped back against a basket of six major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Still, the outlook remained bleak as the U.S. 10-year\par Treasury yield hovered around its highest since July\par 2015. The greenback was not far from a 13-1/2-year peak marked\par on Thursday.    \par     Treasury yields have been rising since \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  won the\par Nov. 8 U.S. presidential election as his policies of more\par government spending are seen pushing up Washington's fiscal\par deficit and inflation.\par     A recent series of solid U.S. economic data has also spurred\par views that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise interest rates more\par next year after a widely expected hike in December.\par     Asia also faces further pressure from Trump's protectionist\par stance on trade due to the region's reliance on exports.\par     "Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to weaken further as the\par dollar has room for more appreciation, given larger fiscal\par spending, increasing pressure on trade and U.S. policy of the\par repatriation of overseas profits," said Jeong My-young, Samsung\par Futures research head in Seoul.\par     "Technically, the USD is seen excessively bought, while all\par other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are seen excessively sold. But markets are\par almost ignoring possibilities of corrections of the trend."\par     For the first time in nine months, sentiment on all of the\par nine emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  covered in a Reuters poll has\par turned bearish, according to the survey published on Thursday.\par  \par     \par     RINGGIT, RUPIAH\par     For the week, Malaysia's ringgit and Indonesia's\par rupiah led depreciation among their regional peers.\par     The ringgit on Friday fell to 4.4640 per dollar, its weakest\par since Sept. 29, 2015, when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a 17-year low.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost 1 percent against the dollar\par so far this week as the government's bond prices \par slid.\par     "It is better to keep long USD holdings. Maybe there is\par another 2-3 percent to run until the year-end," said a senior\par Malaysian bank trader in Kuala Lumpur, when asked whether to buy\par the dollar against the ringgit.\par     The rupiah also has slumped 1 percent this week as foreign\par investors kept selling Jakarta stocks and Indonesia's\par government bonds.\par     India's rupee has skidded 0.5 percent so far this week. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday touched a record low of 68.8650 per dollar\par before recovering on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The yuan has fallen 0.4 percent for the week, poised to\par suffer a third straight week of depreciation.\par     Singapore's dollar has eased 0.4 percent as the\par government downgraded its economic growth and exports for this\par year, reinforcing worries about a possible recession but keeping\par the chance of policy stimulus alive. \par     The Philippine peso has slid 0.3 percent so far\par this week on continuous equity outflows.\par         \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0450 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  113.51         113.34     -0.15\par   Sing dlr                   1.4311         1.4320     +0.06\par   Taiwan dlr                 31.915       