\par\par \b \uc2 India Government Moves to Calm Markets -- Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rajesh Roy   \par \uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 10:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI--India's government said on Friday that the economy was strong enough to deal with the fallout of the U.K. referendum and promised to push forward with policy changes, as it sought to calm investors amid a sharp decline in shares and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Our aim will be to smooth this volatility and minimize its impact on the economy in the short term," Finance Minister Arun Jaitley said in a statement. "At the same time, for the medium term, we will steadfastly pursue our ambitious reform agenda," he added.\par \par \uc2 The country's benchmark S&P \uc2 BSE\uc2  Sensex fell as much as 4% and the rupee weakened 1.4% against the U.S. dollar to its lowest level in nearly four months, tracking deep losses in global markets as investors reacted to the unexpected outcome of the U.K. voting to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Jaitley said India's low inflation, a committment to fiscal discipline and healthy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves make it a safe investment bet for global investors at a time of global turmoil.\par \par \uc2 "As investors look around the world for safe havens in these turbulent times, India stands out both in terms of stability and growth," he said. "Our growth and inflation prospects are further improving in the wake of the good monsoons."\par \par \uc2 Over the past few weeks, New Delhi has tried to attract global investors by easing investment rules in several sectors, approving a plan for its biggest-ever auction of telecom bandwidth and announcing measures to revive the textiles sector, which employs one of the highest number of workers in the country.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Jaitley said the government won't let the policy momentum slow and that it would make renewed efforts to implement the Goods and Services Tax -- billed as one of the biggest indrect tax policy changes by the country in decades. The proposed law, which is pending lawmakers' approval, is key for the economy to grow at its potential of 8% to 9%, he added.\par \par \uc2 Separately speaking to reporters, Economic Affairs Secretary Shaktikanta Das appeared to play down the market's sharp fall, saying that they will stabilize over the next few days as investors move past the outcome of the U.K referendum.\par \par \uc2 The decline in the Indian rupee was in line with its Asian peers and policymakers are ready to use the country's large reserves to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added.\par \par \uc2 "We have enough firepower [\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves] and will use them judiciously to address the situation," he said.\par \par \uc2 India has narrowed its current account deficit from record-high levels in 2013, lowered inflation by about half since then and accelerated policy changes to strengthen its economy, helping reduce its vulnerability to external economic shocks. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have also grown to the highest-ever level of more than $363 billion, providing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  enough ammunition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local markets to ensure stability.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  said the economy's sound economic fundamentals, normal levels of seasonal rainfall expected this year and healthy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves help guard the economy and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act to smoothen market volatility.\par \par \uc2 "Where liquidity is needed, domestic liquidity or foreign liquidity, we will provide a proper amount so there is an orderly adjustment," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rajesh Roy at rajesh.roy@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Gabriele Parussini contributed to this article\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 24, 2016 04:05 ET (08:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160624ec6o0012u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
