\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Tumbles to 4-Month Low on Shock 'Brexit' Result -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 07:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0528 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India's rupee tumbles as much as 1.4% against the haven U.S. dollar, reaching its lowest level in nearly four months, as the market reacted to the unexpected outcome that the U.K. has voted to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . USD/INR spiked to 68.22 compared to its last closing of 67.25, but has since subsided to 68.12. The surprise outcome of the U.K. referendum triggered a surge of haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the U.S. dollar and the Japanese yen, which rose as much as 7.2% versus the greenback. Stock markets around the world fell, with the benchmark Sensex tanking 2.8%, exacerbating the bearish outlook for the rupee. The India rupee has tenatively recouped some of its losses, due to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been selling U.S. dollars to tamp down the rupee's excessive weakening. The falling rupee has implications for India's inflation levels, which will affect the RBI's monetary policy stance in the medium term. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: DJP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0527 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The president of Germany's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ifo Institute\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Clemens Fuest\f28 \uc2 \f2 , called the British vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  "a defeat of reason." He said that politicians must now do whatever they can to limit the economic damage. This involves ensuring that Britain "remains integrated into the single market as much as possible." He said it was important "to conclude negotiations as quickly as possible so that the phase of uncertainty over the future economic relations stays as short as possible." (todd.buell@wsj.com; Twitter: @ToddBuell) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0524 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] This weekend provides a good window for \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to take monetary policy action to help improve sentiment, with Brexit now the apparent outcome of the U.K. referendum, say Raymond Yeung and David Qu, economists with ANZ Research. Next Monday is the regular submission day for the reserve requirement and the tax payment period is coming up, they say. July 5 is the next day for reserve requirement submissions, so market liquidity could tighten in the meantime, they add. (pei.li@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0523 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's government moves to calm markets with assurance that it is prepared along with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to deal with any eventuality resulting out of the UK's exit from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "We and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  have over the past several weeks discussed all possible eventualities of Brexit. We are prepared," Economic Affairs Secretary Shaktikanta Das says. The benchmark S&P \f28 \uc2 \f2 BSE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sensex was last trading down 3.8% at 25,976.51 while the rupee was trading about 1.3% weaker against the U.S. dollar at 68.12. "We have enough firepower and will use them judiciously to address the situation," Das says, referring to the $360 billion of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holds. (rajesh.roy@wsj.com; @rovingrajesh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0523 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Institute of Directors\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a U.K. business group, says it is urging British politicians to press ahead with managing the transition after Thursday's Brexit vote. Simon Walker, the body's director general, describes the immediate aftermath of the vote as "a nervy time for business leaders." "British businesses are resilient and, with their characteristic ingenuity, they will weather this storm," he says in a statement shortly after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 British Broadcasting Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . forecast a vote by Britons to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The institute underscores a key worry for business in the U.K.--its ability to hold on to current European employees and continue to recruit them in the future. "One thing the Government must do immediately is to guarantee the right to remain of \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  citizens currently in the UK. Companies do not want to have to worry about losing valued staff," Walker says. (chip.cummins@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0522 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's exports to the U.K. and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  may tumble during the next few months with Britain voting to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 , according to the most recent forecasts. Somkiat Triratpan, director of the ministry's trade policy and strategy office at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai Commerce Ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2 , says that the worrying consequence of the "Brexit" vote is the weakening of the British pound and the euro, which will result in a rise in Thai export prices to these markets. However, Thailand has already shifted to focusing on trade expansion to more countries, adds Mr. Somkiat. Thailand's exports to \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  currently represent around 9.0% of total exports while shipments to the UK account for about 1.0-2.0%, he says. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@wsj.com; Twitter: @nopbkk) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TRL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0520 GMT Sonja Marten of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the GBP to slide further, saying a move by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  to lower interest rates would make sense. Financial markets need to brace themselves for long periods of high uncertainty, even if Friday's extreme market volatility tapers off. "A return to normal conditions isn't expected over the short term," she says. There is no tried and trusted guide for an \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  member's exit, and it isn't clear what Brexit supporters want. Europe will need to avoid being too lenient with the U.K. to avoid sending a potentially fatal signal to other \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  members with waning support for membership, she notes. "For the next days, officials will focus on calming markets," she adds. (nikki.houston@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0514 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japan's finance minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taro Aso\f28 \uc2 \f2  warns of possible "firm action" on the surging yen, but his remarks have no noticeable impact on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a sign of skepticism among investors that Tokyo has the determination to override Washington's objection to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . This could add to pressure on Aso to carry out the threat to dispel speculation that he is all bark and no bite. Allowing further gains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could risk sinking the whole project of Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  to bring the economy back to prosperity by dealing a deadly blow to exports. Aso reiterates that he will "more intensely and carefully" monitor exchange rates, but however strongly he emphasizes his vigilance, it will be of little use if the markets don't listen to him. (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0513 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  say they now expect the UK's vote to depart the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  will prompt \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  to ease policy more than expected. "Our forecast already anticipated further easing in September, in the form of an extension of the current asset purchase program through end-2017," they said. "We now expect additional easing involving a 10bp cut in the deposit rate...and a further extension of asset purchases into 2018," they said. Still, "We do not expect these additional moves to come quickly, unless financial markets put \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  under a lot of pressure." (todd.buell@wsj.com; @ToddBuell) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: DJP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0512 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fortescue Metals Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s (FMG.AU) strides in reducing its debt pile have "created a substantial buffer for the company to maintain leverage metrics at adequate levels for its rating," even if iron-ore prices fall, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It reiterates the miner's rating at Ba3 and changes the outlook for Fortescue to stable from negative. While \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  "expects the price environment for iron ore to continue to remain volatile with risk to the downside, Fortescue has generated free cash flow in excess of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  previous expectations and has used such cash to reduce its overall indebtedness," it says. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0511 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (8306.TO) says Friday that the U.K. vote to exit the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  won't likely impact MUFG's core business. "We don't believe that the effects of (Brexit) will cause fundamental change to our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  foundations," the country's biggest lender said. MUFG also said it has no intention to withdraw from the U.K. despite the results, but it anticipates certain impact such as an economic downturn in the U.K. and \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and the U.K.'s withdrawal from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  passport scheme. MUFG is now down 10% at Y462. (atsuko.fukase@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0510 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The "leave" result isn't good news for the tech sector either in the U.K. or in Europe, according to one of the U.K.'s most valuable private tech startups, international payments firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 TransferWise Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The U.K. has the strongest tech scene [in Europe], so it's played a significant role in attracting talent and investors to the whole region. That's unlikely to continue," says a spokeswoman for the London-based fintech firm, valued at over $1 billion. "The whole of the European tech ecosystem will feel the impact," she adds. \f28 \uc2 \f2 TransferWise\f28 \uc2 \f2  makes international money transfers at cheaper rates than typical banks. It stopped allowing customers to swap British pounds for other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday evening, citing possible volatility. It said it planned to resume transfers Friday. (telis.demos@wsj.com, @telisdemos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 24, 2016 01:28 ET (05:28 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160624ec6o000mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
