\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -India rupee falls on Rajan's surprise decision to step down; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  up\b0\par\par\uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2016\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupee near 1-month lows; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted\par     * Rajan resignation sparks doubt on reforms, inflation fight\par     * Other EM Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains on hopes Britain will stay in \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, June 20 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee lost ground\par on Monday as the country's well-regarded \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor\par unexpectedly decided to step down, prompting doubts over future\par efforts to reform policies and tame inflation.\par     Other emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , by contrast, rose as\par sentiment improved on growing hopes that Britain will vote to\par stay in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Spot rupee lost as much as 0.9 percent to 67.70 per\par dollar, its weakest since May 24, before recovering some losses\par with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected to support the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     In non-deliverable forwards markets, the Indian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slid to near one-month lows versus the greenback.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's "rock star" governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Raghuram\par Rajan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , feted by foreign investors but under pressure from\par political opponents at home, stunned government officials and\par colleagues on Saturday by announcing he would step down when his\par three-year term ends on Sept. 4. \par     "This is a negative surprise as markets (and we) were\par expecting him to continue," Nomura analysts said in a note. "Dr.\par Rajan added credibility to the RBI and there is no obvious\par successor of a similar stature."\par     "There is also a risk of some delay in unfinished reforms\par such as formation of a monetary policy committee, bank\par restructuring and allowing repo transactions in the corporate\par bond markets," they wrote.\par     Rajan, a former chief economist at the International\par Monetary Fund, is held in high esteem by many for overhauling\par the way the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  operates.\par     Some foreign investors had already been concerned over his\par possible resignation and India's bond market had a bond outflow\par of $656 million in May. \par     "Foreign investors will likely offload additional bond\par investments, especially longer-tenors on sentiment and\par heightened uncertainty around the RBI's long term inflation\par targeting policy," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note.\par     Rajan pushed for inflation targeting to tackle India's\par history of volatile prices, which was made law by the government\par last year.\par     \par     EM ASIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UP\par     South Korea's won led gains among emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as Seoul shares jumped 1.5 percent, outpacing\par regional equity markets.\par     The won rose 1.1 percent to 1,160.3 per dollar, its\par strongest since June 10.\par     The Indonesian rupiah advanced 0.7 percent to\par 13,240 to the greenback, its strongest since June 9, with most\par government bond prices up.\par     Malaysia's ringgit appreciated 0.9 percent to\par 4.0640, its firmest since June 10.\par     Risk sentiment improved as three British opinion polls \par ahead of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  membership referendum on June 23 showed the\par "Remain" camp recovering some momentum, although the overall\par picture remained one of an evenly split electorate. \par  \par     Still, trading stayed lacklustre in emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets as anxiety grew before the referendum.\par     "Markets seemed cautious ahead of the Brexit vote. Both\par client flows and trading interest were light due to\par uncertainties," said a senior Malaysian bank trader in Kuala\par Lumpur.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0500 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  104.66         104.10     -0.54\par   Sing dlr                   1.3435         1.3486     +0.38\par   Taiwan dlr                 32.244         32.385     +0.44\par   Korean won                1161.00        1172.70     +1.01\par   Baht                        35.20          35.25     +0.14\par   Peso                       46.340         46.445     +0.23\par   Rupiah                      13260          13335     +0.57\par   Rupee                       67.36          67.08     -0.41\par   Ringgit                    4.0715         4.1000     +0.70\par   Yuan                       6.5784         6.5900     +0.18\par                                                             \par   Change so far in 2016                                     \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End prev year  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  104.66        