\par\par \b \uc2 India's cenbank buys net $1.34 bln in spot  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  in April, below March levels\b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2016\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 10 (Reuters) - \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $1.34 billion in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in April, sharply below a net purchase of $4.69 billion in March, according to its monthly bulletin released on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures markets amounted to $260 million, both on the buy and sell sides, the bulletin showed.\par \par \uc2 In spot markets, the RBI bought $2.64 billion and sold $1.3 billion in April when the rupee moved in a band of 66.07-66.8475 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves that month went up by $3.36 billon, partly due to the RBI's spot \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The RBI's net outstanding forward dollar sales stood at $4.05 billion as of the end of April, little changed from $4.25 billion in the previous month, the bulletin showed. (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury; Editing by Subhranshu Sahu)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-13T12:18:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160610ec6a011t5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
