\par\par \b \uc2 Morning News Call - India, December 10\b0\par\par\uc2 931 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2015\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To access the newsletter, click on the link:\par  \par  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_12102015.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_12102015.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par         \par          \par     FACTORS TO WATCH\par     10.00 am: Special Secretary Ajay Narayan Jha to speak at conference of state\par governments.\par     10.30 am: Junior Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jayant Sinha\f28 \uc2 \f2  to speak at an event.\par     11.00 am: Winter session of parliament continues.\par     \par     \par     GMF ASIA - FED FOCUS- Join Oliver Pursche, CEO, Bruderman Brothers and a\par member of the Harvard Business Review Advisory Council, to discuss Fed\par expectations and the state of the U.S. economy. To join the conversation click\par on the link \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://forms.thomsonreuters.com/communities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://forms.thomsonreuters.com/communities/}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par     \par     INDIA TOP NEWS\par      Indian inflation seen above 5 pct in Nov, room for more rate cuts\par narrowing\par India's retail inflation rate likely rose above the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par medium-term 5 percent target in November as food prices climbed, leaving little\par room for more interest rate cuts, a Reuters poll found. \par      Investors hover as e-tailers boost demand for Indian warehouses\par Overseas firms including Dutch pension fund manager APG and U.S. buyout group\par Warburg Pincus are looking to invest in India's warehouses, hoping to cash in on\par demand for modern and efficient storage space from booming online retailers.\par  \par      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  futures markets - traders\par The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the rupee \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  futures market, a\par senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official told a gathering of bank trainees last week,\par according to four people briefed on the comments. \par      Indian temple set to give government's gold scheme a boost\par One of the most popular temples in India may soon make the first substantial\par contribution to Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's plan to recycle tonnes of idle\par bullion to reduce imports and the country's current account deficit.\par  \par      India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alkem Laboratories\f28 \uc2 \f2  $200 mln IPO fully subscribed - exchanges\par Indian drugmaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alkem Laboratories\f28 \uc2 \f2  filled the order book for its $200 million\par initial public offering in the second day of book-building after attracting\par strong demand from institutional investors, according to exchanges data.\par  \par     \par     \par     GLOBAL TOP NEWS\par      Australian jobs surge by most in 15 years, stir doubts about data\par Australian employment surged by the most in over 15 years in November and nudged\par the unemployment rate to a 19-month low, but so stunning was the result that it\par revived doubts about the reliability of the data. \par      Chinese investors warm to foreign stocks to shelter from local chill\par It has taken a slump in the property market, a white-knuckle ride on local\par shares and a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation, but China's retail investors are finally\par taking a serious look at overseas stocks and bonds. \par      Muslim proposal prompts calls to ban Trump from UK, Israel\par Israeli politicians and more than 370,000 Britons urged their governments on\par Wednesday to bar Donald Trump from their countries after the Republican\par presidential front-runner said Muslims should be denied entry into the United\par States. \par     \par     \par     LOCAL MARKETS OUTLOOK\par     (As reported by NewsRise)\par      The SGX Nifty Futures was trading at 7,655.50, up 0.12 percent from its\par previous close.\par      The Indian rupee will likely edge lower against the U.S. dollar, as a\par recent slump and continued weakness in oil price deepens concerns of a global\par slowdown. Bets that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will soon raise interest rates are also\par likely to damp demand for risk assets.\par      Indian government bonds are likely to edge lower, as investors defer\par purchases ahead of a string of key developments over the next few days including\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision on interest rates. The yield on the\par benchmark 7.72 percent bond maturing in 2025 is likely to trade in a 7.76\par percent-7.81 percent range.\par     \par     \par     GLOBAL MARKETS\par      U.S. stocks closed lower on Wednesday in a choppy session as oil resumed\par its decline, fuelling investor worries about global economic growth and causing\par the S&P 500 index to track the move in the commodity. \par      Asian stocks slipped as weak oil prices continued to feed global growth\par worries, while the euro held solid gains after a policymaker poured cold water\par on market expectations of more easing by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par      The euro held on to solid gains early and stayed above the $1.10 big\par figure after comments from a central banker suggested markets had been expecting\par too much stimulus from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par      \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  debt prices rose on Wednesday in thin volume, as a fall in\par oil prices and on the stock market prompted investors to seek safe-haven\par government bonds. \par      Crude oil prices edged up early, supported by a fall in U.S. crude\par inventories after 10 straight weeks of builds, but a global oversupply and cheap\par oil are still dominating the broader market. \par      Gold was treading water as investors stuck to the sidelines ahead of a\par widely anticipated U.S. rate hike next week, with even a slump in the dollar\par failing to trigger interest in the metal. \par     \par     \par  MARKETS            CLOSE         FII INVESTMENTS  EQUITIES       DEBT\par  PNDF spot          66.88/66.91   December 9        -$78.80 mln   -$17.36 mln\par  10-yr bond yield   7.79 pct      Month-to-date     -$696.11 mln  -$168.54 mln\par                                   Year-to-date       $2.92 bln     $9.32 bln\par  \par     \par     \par     For additional data:\par     India govt bond market volumes       \par     Stock market reports                 \par     Non-deliverable forwards data        \par     Corporate debt stories               [IN CORPD]\par     Local market closing/intraday levels [IN SNAPSHOT]\par     Monthly inflows                      [INFLOWS RTRS TABLE IN]\par  \par \par \par ($1 = 66.83 Indian rupees)\par \par  (Reporting by Samarendra Sahoo in Bengaluru)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-12-10T04:20:51.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151210ebca00337\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
