\par\par \b \uc2 3 Things Learned From India's Sell-Off -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shuli Ren   \par \uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2015\par 06:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 In the second-quarter, India's rupee lost 2.7%, recently trading at 63.96 per dollar, while the \uc2 S&P\uc2  BSE 100 Index has retreated 3.9%.\par \par \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2 's economists Indranil Sen Gupta and Abhishek Gupta have three top-down lessons learned from the retreat.\par \par \uc2 First, India's stock market has transformed from a "hope trade" to a "show-me trade." The March quarter's earnings are anemic again and investors now want to see solid evidence that India is in a cyclical recovery. Instead of fussing over how the GST tax bills are doing in the Parliament, lending rate cuts are more important. "A lending rate cut takes about 6 months to support growth," while "the impact of reforms will be felt only in 5-10 years." As such, we need to pay attention to whether Indian banks are indeed cutting their commercial lending rates after the benchmark rate cuts by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Second, don't bet on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  till the rupee hits 65 per dollar, for two reasons. First, the rupee always seasonally weakens between April and September. Second, Governor Rajan "will understandably want to hoard precious \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to fight any contagion" when the Federal Reserve Bank raises interest rates. \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  expects the Fed to raise rates in September.\par \par \uc2 Third, foreign debt investors are more patient, still holding onto India's debt because they are expecting more rate cuts, which would affect government bonds a lot more directly than equities:\par \par \uc2 Debt FIIs have shown greater faith in RBI rate expectations than equity investors who have been offloading bank stocks. FII debt investors still remain bullish on Indian bonds in view of hopes of capital gains on RBI rate cuts, and consequently, softer yields.\par \par \uc2 Checking in on prices, India's stock market gained with the rest of Asia, with the BSE 100 Index up 1.4% recently. \uc2 Tata Motors\uc2  ( TTM) rose 3.3%, \uc2 ICICI Bank\uc2  ( IBN) gained 2.7%, \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  ( HDB) rose 2.3%.\par \par \uc2 This quarter, the \uc2 WisdomTree India Earnings Fund\uc2  ( EPI) has fallen 7%, the iShares MSCI India ETF (INDA) dropped 7.7%, \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Asia Stocks to Watch blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/asiastocks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/asiastocks/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Access Investor Kit for \f28 \uc2 \f2 HDFC Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=INE040A01026"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=INE040A01026}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Access Investor Kit for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Motors Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=INE155A01022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=INE155A01022}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Access Investor Kit for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US0605051046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US0605051046}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Access Investor Kit for \f28 \uc2 \f2 HDFC Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \