\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-India's record  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  warchest set for Fed rate hike test\b0\par\par\uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 22:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats Thursday story with no changes)\par \par \uc2 * RBI builds up record \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $338 billion\par \par \uc2 * Looming U.S. rate hike could prompt emerging market sell-off\par \par \uc2 * RBI reserves considered enough to cushion India -source\par \par \uc2 * India chastened by capital flight in 2013 "taper tantrum"\par \par \uc2 By Suvashree Choudhury and Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 19 (Reuters) - Chastened by a tumble in the rupee in 2013 at the prospect of tighter U.S. monetary policy, India has built up record \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of nearly $340 billion to insulate the economy from capital flight as the United States prepares to lift interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of India Governor \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  has long warned of the risk to emerging economies when the U.S. Federal Reserve makes the first rise in its zero percent interest rates since the 2008 financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 He has also been actively buying dollars, helped by a net inflow of $54 billion of foreign money since the start of 2014, which has driven shares to record highs and pushed bond yields sharply lower.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has seen reserves rise by about a quarter since the end of 2013 to $338 billion and headed off a sharp appreciation in the rupee. That gives him the firepower to limit a slide in the rupee and any dislocation in domestic markets if foreign money rushes out.\par \par \uc2 "As of now, we have accumulated enough reserves," said a policy maker familiar with the RBI's thinking.\par \par \uc2 "The Governor has created that space to face a U.S. rate hike," he added. "Adding to reserves was an objective last year. This year it is more to contain volatility."\par \par \uc2 Those preparations look set to be tested in the coming months after the Fed removed a reference to being "patient" on interest rates from its policy statement on Wednesday, paving the way for a hike within months, though it also signalled it was in no rush to push borrowing costs higher.\par \par \uc2 In 2013, when he was an economic adviser to the \uc2 Indian finance ministry\uc2 , Rajan witnessed firsthand the perils of being unprepared, when concerns about the Fed scaling back its monetary stimulus sparked a "taper tantrum" that roiled emerging markets, saddling India with its worst market turmoil in more than two decades.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry were seen by markets as unprepared and hesitant in their initial reaction.\par \par \uc2 Rajan, formerly chief economist at the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , was credited with a key role in rescuing India from that crisis with measures that helped stem foreign selling.\par \par \uc2 Rajan said on Wednesday India now had "comfortable" \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and its current account deficit was under control.\par \par \uc2 INDIA SHINING\par \par \uc2 India has seen a resurgence in investor popularity since the election of a reform-minded government under Prime Minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , helped by improving economic fundamentals and the RBI's efforts to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 It also imposed curbs on gold imports in 2013, a measure that, combined with the slump in crude prices, helped substantially narrow the country's current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 India has subsequently attracted more foreign capital than the "Fragile Five" countries to which it is often compared, but the RBI considers such inflows a double-edged sword, since they leave it at the whim of global investors\par \par \uc2 India saw net foreign investments of nearly $20 billion in 2007, ahead of the global financial crisis, only to see investors pull out $9.4 billion the next year.\par \par \uc2 And in 2013, $8 billion flowed out of its debt markets, sending the rupee to a record low of 68.85 per dollar in August.\par \par \uc2 As a result, Rajan has pushed hard to build up \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which had fallen as low as $274.8 billion in September 2013, enough to account for just under seven months of imports, the lowest import cover since 1996.\par \par \uc2 With the rupee about 10 percent above the 2013 low, the governor can keep adding to those reserves by buying dollars, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI enjoys pretty decent headroom in terms of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  they can do," said \uc2 Siddhartha Sanyal\uc2 , chief \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist for \uc2 Barclays\uc2 . (Writing by Rafael Nam; Editing by Will Waterman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-19T22:00:00.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150319eb3j00rby\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
