\par\par \b \uc2 Reliance Stock Recovering on $750 Million Bond Issue -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 3,141 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2015\par 06:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0512 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  ] \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) stock is recovering from early losses to trade up 0.1% at 938.15 rupees a share after it said Wednesday it had issued bonds worth $750 million, paying an interest of 4.875%. The stock had earlier fallen to 932.20 rupees in early trade Wednesday. Reliance is due to buy these bonds back in 2045. The oil and gas major is paying the lowest interest rate ever paid by an Asian private corporate issuer for a 30-year issuance, Reliance said. The issue was over subscribed over 3.07 times across 167 bidders, Reliance said. (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH\f28 \par \par \uc2 Corrections & amplifications\par \par \uc2 Market headline was corrected at 0540 GMT. The original incorrectly stated the issuance as $750.\par \par \uc2 0512 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  ] Lower commodity prices could translate into A$500 billion in forgone earnings for Australia over the years to 2025, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said Wednesday. The outlook for revenues from Australian liquefied natural gas, and bulk commodities shipments--which account for almost half of total export earnings--has deteriorated significantly, it said. Tim Toohey, chief economist at Goldman Sachs said overall export revenues are still forecast to increase over the coming years--underpinned by a strong outlook for physical shipments, particularly for gas. Still, the impact of lower prices will hit the economy hard, cutting tax revenues, damping confidence and driving higher unemployment, he says. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter: @JamesGlynnWSJ) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0510 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] USD/THB is surprisingly stable near its Tuesday closing level of 32.59, despite regional USD/Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs all sliding on broad U.S. dollar weakness and a return of investor risk-taking. One likely explanation is that \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  may be supporting the pair to prevent excessive baht strength. A trader said the BOT was suspected of capping the baht around 32.50 on Tuesday--possibly attempting to prevent the triggering of stoploss orders past the 200-day moving average line at 32.45. The BOT could be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well today, judging from the unusually firm USD/THB stance. A resurgence of the euro overnight--on the possibility that Greece renegotiation of its debt obligations could take months--depressed the U.S. dollar index and triggered a reaction in most parts of Asia Wednesday. USD/THB is now 32.57 from its last close of 32.59. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0510 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Slight improvement in Singapore's PMI reported overnight boosts the local dollar on Wednesday, with USD/SGD currently at 1.3446 versus 1.3524 late in Asia on Tuesday. Singapore reports overall manufacturing PMI at 49.9 in January, versus 49.6 in December. Electronics PMI stays unchanged at 50.5 in January. "With Singapore's manufacturing PMIs coming in a touch better than prior expectations, the broadly weaker dollar should translate into a heavier tone for the USD/SGD in the near term," OCBC says in a note. The house tips the pair in an easier 1.3400-1.3500 range on Wednesday. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0454 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500325.BY), owner of the world's biggest crude oil refining complex, has raised $750 million through senior unsecured notes due 2045. The notes will be denominated in US dollars, and will bear fixed interest of 4.875%, with interest payable semi-annually in arrears The funds will be used for the company's ongoing capital expenditures. The notes were more than 3.07 times over-subscribed across 167 accounts. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Bank PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup Global Markets Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  acted as joint managers. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Tuesday assigned a Baa2 senior unsecured foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  debt rating with a stable outlook to the issuance.(saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0446 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The USD/CNY is lower today, tracking guidance set by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Wednesday. The pair is now at 6.2491, vs Tuesday's close at 6.2581. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set central parity at 6.1318 vs Tuesday parity at 6.1369. A weaker reading for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  China services purchasing managers index, which fell to a six-month low at 51.8 in January vs 53.4 in December, didn't manage to offset the stronger yuan Wednesday. In recent weeks, the yuan has been weakening and is likely to trend lower as there are wide expectations for Beijing to continue to ease monetary policy with liquidity injections as well as cuts to banks' reserve requirements and to interest rates, to prevent a sharper-than-expected economic slowdown. Offshore, one-year USD/CNY NDFs are up at 6.3805 from 6.2718 late Tuesday. (esther.fung@wsj.com, @estherfung) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0439 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The credit quality of China's big state energy companies remains stable despite a sharp downturn in global oil prices, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  . Support from China's government, strong liquidity and more conservative capital expenditure than previously are among the reasons the ratings agency says it is holding steady at Aa3 its ratings of the country's big three state-owned oil-and-gas producers, \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  (parent of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroChina\f28 \uc2 \f2  [0857.HK]), China Petrochemical parent of Sinopec [0386.HK], and \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Offshore Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  (0883.HK). \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says infusions of private money as part of the government's mixed-ownership reform plans will help offset weakness in the companies' exploration-and-production business segments. (brian.spegele@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0436 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it now expects \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut interest rates to 2.0% in May, saying the impact of falling commodity prices on the economy is likely to be vast. "There are significant impacts back through to the real economy. Lower export earnings result in lower profits, lower tax receipts, lower investment and lower employment," says Tim Toohey, chief economist at Goldman Sachs , Australia. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  continues to forecast GDP growth of just 2.0% in 2015, but it has downgraded expectations for 2016-18. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: DMF \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0432 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The combination of slower growth in Australia, low interest rates for longer and deteriorating fiscal and trade balances provide scope for the Australian dollar to move lower in 2015 than previously forecast, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a research note. Tim Toohey, chief economist at Goldmans said he now expects the Aussie will move to US$0.7200 on a 12-month view, from US$0.7500 previously. The forecast revision follows an unexpected cut in interest rates by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Tuesday. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0419 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Copper extended gains in Asia trade, after posting overnight one of the biggest daily gains in nearly two years. Investors are betting that a slowdown in China's manufacturing sector, the latest in a stream of weak economic data, would prompt the nation to cut rates and announce new spending on infrastructure. Three-month copper prices on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Metal Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  were at $5,687/ton, up from the opening price of $5,680/ton.(biman.mukherji@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: DMF \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0416 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The improvement in China's housing market so far appears to be limited to some cities, with housing sales in January falling month-on-month in 38 out of the 41 cities tracked by China Real Estate Index System. With the Lunar New Year Festival in February typically a slower time for home-buying, month-on-month sales figures in February could still be sluggish, the data provider says. On a year-on-year basis, housing sales rose in 22 out of 41 cities, with growth in sales in Shenzhen, Hangzhou, Zhongshan, Haikou and Jinan outpacing the rest. Nationwide housing sales in the whole of 2014 fell 7.8% by value from 2013, prompting worries about an entrenched correction that would further drag economic growth. The central and local governments have been stepping up efforts to prop up the country's all-important property market, including removing administrative limits on multiple home purchases and easing monetary policy. (esther.fung@wsj.com, Twitter: @estherfung) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0413 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Vietnam will likely soon raise its retail electricity prices as the country is seeking to bring the prices to a market-based level, the Ministry of Industry and Trade said. It said electricity production cost remains below prices, discouraging private investment in new power plants. The ministry said that state-owned Vietnam Electricity Group, the country' sole electricity distributor, has proposed raising prices by an average of 9.5%. Analysts said Vietnam's easing inflation is giving room for the government to raise prices. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4 Feb 2015 00:39 ET \par Correction to Reliance Stock Recovering Market Talk\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  issued a bond worth $750 million. The headline on "Reliance Stock Recovering on $750 Bond Issue -- Market Talk," at 0512 GMT, incorrectly stated the issuance as $750 instead of $750 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0532 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] USD/INR has been immune to the broad U.S. dollar drop in Asia Wednesday but it might be a fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that is keeping it propped up. An offshore trader said he expects the RBI might step in around 61.50; USD/INR is currently trading at 61.63 from its Tuesday close of 61.59. The RBI had said in its post-monetary policy meeting statement on Tuesday that it has recently been dampening rupee volatility via market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But the broad overnight weakness of the U.S. dollar--due to a strong rebound of the euro as well as the Australia dollar--may persuade the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to loosen its reins on the rupee. The daily chart could turn bearish for USD/INR on a Wednesday close below 61.46, the entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend channel, and spur U.S. dollar selling by short-term speculators. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0523 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The unexpected break of USD/SGD below 1.3500 is leading to a sharp drop in the pair on Wednesday, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Overseas Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  suggests in a note that the pair may even hit 1.3430. "Downward momentum is gaining rapidly...Only a move back above 1.3500/05 would indicate that the downward pressure has eased," the bank says. The pair is currently at 1.3445 after quoting as low as 1.3437. That compares with 1.3524 late in Asia on Tuesday. UOB estimates that on a trade-weighted basis, the Singapore dollar's nominal effective exchange rate is trading at 0.9% below the mid-point of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy band this morning. The bank expects the pair to trade between 0.5% and 1.0% below the mid-point today, implying a USD/SGD range of 1.3403-1.3470 based on current levels. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0522 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Indonesia's economic growth likely moderated in the fourth quarter of last year due to weaker private consumption following around 30% increase in subsidized fuel prices in late November that prompted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tighten further its monetary stance. Lingering political uncertainties even after a new government was established likely also continued to make investors to hold up investment plans. The median forecast of 11 economists polled by the Wall Street Journal is for 4.95% year-on-year growth in the fourth quarter, compared with 5.01% in the third quarter. While for the full 2014, they expect the economy to have grown 5.07%, slowing from 5.78% in 2013. "We expect GDP growth to bounce back to circa 5.5% in 2015 on the back of higher fiscal spending this year," says DBS's economist Gundy Cahyadi. The official statistics agency will release the GDP data Thursday around 0400 GMT. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0515 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The NZX-50 finished up 0.1% at 5785.319 as strength in the Australian market offset falls in the energy stocks after ratings downgrades from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  , says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Craigs Investment Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  broker Belinda Stanley. She adds the ratings downgrade likely prompted some profit taking in the energy stocks with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Meridian Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MELCA.NZ) finishing down 1.8% at NZ$1.955, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Contact Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  (CEN.NZ) was down 1.4% at NZ$7.20 and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mighty River Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MRP.NZ) 0.6% lower at NZ$3.47. Spark NZ (SPK.NZ) ended the session up 2.7% at NZ$3.46 after the company announced a joint venture with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vocus Communications\f28 \uc2 \f2  to increase its fiber network. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com;Twitter: @lucy_craymer) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0515 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reiterates that the country's negative headline inflation isn't a sign of deflation and doesn't have an impact on financial stability. In fact, it's positive for Thailand's economic rebound as falling oil prices lower production and transportation costs, lending support to domestic demand, says Mathee Supapongse, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Assistant Governor. He adds that there's no sign that consumers have postponed investments or purchases of goods based on expectations that the prices will further slide. "We aren't concerned because [negative inflation] isn't caused by sluggish demand...prices of other products still go up," Mathee says. "It's a supply shock from falling oil prices." BOT expects headline inflation, which includes volatile items like energy and food, to be in the negative until the second quarter this year, but to pick up later.(warangkana.chomchuen@wsj.com; Twitter: @waanspeaking) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0512 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500325.BY) stock is recovering from early losses to trade up 0.1% at 938.15 rupees a share after it said Wednesday it had issued bonds worth $750 million, paying an interest of 4.875%. The stock had earlier fallen to 932.20 rupees in early trade Wednesday. Reliance is due to buy these bonds back in 2045. The oil and gas major is paying the lowest interest rate ever paid by an Asian private corporate issuer for a 30-year issuance, Reliance said. The issue was over subscribed over 3.07 times across 167 bidders, Reliance said. (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0512 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Lower commodity prices could translate into A$500 billion in forgone earnings for Australia over the years to 2025, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. The outlook for revenues from Australian liquefied natural gas, and bulk commodities shipments--which account for almost half of total export earnings--has deteriorated significantly, it said