\par\par \b \uc2 India Imported Crude Oil Prices Rise -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2015\par 08:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0736 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India's oil ministry said the price of its imported crude-oil basket rose to $45.33 a barrel Thursday from $43.36 Thursday, reflecting volatility in global crude prices. Oil futures took a breather from a selloff in Asian trade Friday as investors looked for signs of tighter supply that could stem further declines in oil prices. On Thursday, \uc2 OPEC\uc2  lowered its forecast for oil supply growth from non-OPEC members, but it also cut its forecast for world oil demand growth in 2015 by 70,000 barrels a day from its last report. A fall in oil prices is positive for India as it imports three-quarters of its energy needs. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @journosaurabh) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0734 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] It is doubtful the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 , in suddenly letting its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise against the euro, wanted to cause so much pain. But it likely did so knowing the ECB was poised to launch a new bond-buying program in the hopes of stimulating the region's struggling economy. That move would probably weaken the euro against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the bank would effectively be printing euros to buy bonds. But since the Swiss had committed to not allowing the franc to strengthen, the bank would have to sell francs and buy euros. The result would be the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ends up holding billions of dollars in the very \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  its trying to fight against, in this case, the euro. For the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that would mean 43% of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investments were in euros, leaving it with a huge exposure to a decline in the euro. (ken.brown@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0723 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's scapping of its cap for the franc-euro will hurt exports and the economy, but is unlikely to push the country into recession, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "If the euro-franc settles at current levels, Swiss export growth could come to a standstill this year, implying that GDP growth could be 0.5% to a maximum of 1%," says economist Maxime Botteron. The bank had previously forecast 2015 growth of 1.6%. "However, given still good momentum in the domestic economy the risk of a recession in Switzerland looks very low to us," he argues. EUR/CHF was last at 1.0198. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0712 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] NTPC (532555.BY), India's largest power generation utility, has signed for a 100 billion rupee loan agreement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500112.BY). The loan, which has a tenure of 15 years, will be utilized to part finance the company's capital expenditure programme, the power company said in a statement. NTPC has a total electricity generation capacity of 43.12 gigawatts and plans to have a generation capacity of 128 gigawatts by 2032. NTPC shares are trading 0.57% higher at 140.05 rupees on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombay Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 , while the benchmark index is almost flat. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @journosaurabh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0707 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY will likely be well-supported around 115 for some time, with dip-buying at that level as long as expectations for the U.S. economy remain unchanged, says Minori Uchida, chief market analyst at global markets research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\f28 \uc2 \f2  UFJ. But if expectations for eventual rate increases recede in the wake of upcoming U.S. economic indicators for January, the dollar may fall below 115 toward 114 or 113. Uchida says the USD at around Y110 would be consistent with the gap between U.S. and Japanese bond yields. Expectations for the U.S. economy and the likelihood of ECB easing inflate the USD at prevailing rates. While the former have been tempering, an actual ECB decision as early as next week may translate into slight USD selling after the market digests the headlines. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0705 GMT (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) Scheduled government bond issuance in the eurozone is set to slow somewhat next week after two very busy weeks. Hence, Spain is one of the most likely candidates to use the current benign primary [government bond] market environment with a new syndicated 10-year deal, say \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists. A further factor in favor of the possible timing is that the 10-year maturity wouldn't face any scheduled peer pressure next week. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0703 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Banks are still coming to terms with the trading losses arising from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's abrupt decision to scrap the cap on the Swiss franc Thursday. Some banks have apparently resorted to cancelling deals that clients executed on the electronic trading platforms--at the risk of losing these customers. The platforms weren't fast enough to widen their spreads--the gap between the buy and sell rates for EUR/CHF--because such an adjustment typically requires human input. Market chatter is that a second-tier bank has chalked up losses of around $50 million just on trades executed over the e-commerce platform. A top-tier bank would arguably have lost significantly more. One trader said some of these banks have negotiated with customers to adjust the rate at which their stoploss orders were 'filled'--in favor of the bank. Clients' orders to sell EUR/CHF in the event of a break of the 1.2000 floor would have been impossible to execute at a fair rate due to the sudden loss of bids in the market when the SNB stepped away from 3 years of artificially propping it up. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0703 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Once U.S. crude prices fall below $40/barrel or thereabouts, oil production will start shutting down in North America and the North Sea, James Hubbard, head of Asian oil research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. "Below $40 you can look for about 1.5 million barrels a day of supply to be cash flow negative," he says. He says eventually some of the current oversupply will start to disappear pretty quickly. "We might not be at the bottom now at around $45. [Prices] could go down another $10 ... but we're close," he says. February \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nymex\f28 \uc2 \f2  crude is up $0.32 at $46.57/barrel, March Brent crude rose $0.32 to $48.59/barrel. (eric.yep@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0646 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The NZD/USD is trading slightly higher as market focus remains on the unexpected decision by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to remove the cap on the EUR/CHF, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Western Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  Business Solutions Corporate Dealing Manager Chris Hunter. "It has allowed the Kiwi to jump and hold gains other majors simply because they're obviously on the back foot against the Swiss franc." The pair is at 0.7833 vs. 0.7817 early this morning. Hunter puts support for the pair at 0.7790 with resistance coming in at 0.7890. Hunter says markets will now look to U.S. inflation to see if it can offset weakness in the USD/CHF. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com;\f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @lucy_craymer) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: AAP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0615 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  lowers its forecasts for Swiss gross domestic product growth this year and next as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to scrap its cap for the franc-euro will drag on exports and the economy. \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  now sees growth in 2015 at just 0.5%, compared with its previous forecast of 1.8%. For 2016, it now expects growth of 1.1%, down from a previous forecast of 1.7%. "Industry wise, watch exporters are likely to be most negatively affected given a high share of franc-based costs," says Chief Investment Officer Mark Haefele. "Banks also have a high share of franc costs, while client assets are predominantly denominated in euros and dollars," he notes. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0545 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japanese retail \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investors, known collectively as "Mrs. Watanabe," appear to be suffering losses after unprecedented swings in the CHF, following a surprise move by Switzerland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday to scrap its policy of capping the CHF against the EUR. Industry sources say that Japan's financial authorities are conducting hearings into how much individual investors have lost, including their initial margin deposits and amounts paid by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  margin trading firms on behalf of their customers. An \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  margin trading firm manager says the amount of losses individual investors might not be so huge since USD/JPY trading dominates about 80% of their trading. The manager estimates losses for retail investors stemming from the CHF movements could be as much as Y1 billion in total. "The move was historically unprecedented in terms of the degree of change within an hour," the manager says. The EUR/CHF plunged about 30% within a hour. Price volatility was exaggerated when all interbank traders stopped displaying bids-and-offers for a period. (tatsuo.ito@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0539 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/INR is lower than its Thursday close of 62.06, implying a stronger rupee versus the U.S. dollar, but speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is keeping it from gaining too fast may be holding USD/INR back for now. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday--after cutting its repo rate to make it cheaper for banks to borrow money--to quell the rupee's 1.0% gain, says an offshore trader. The RBI could still be lurking around, supporting the bids in USD/INR around its current level of 61.92. If, however, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steps away and USD/INR closes Friday below the 61.68 floor of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone, a bearish-dollar technical signal will be activated. Chart-motivated traders could then be encouraged to short the dollar versus the rupee for a near-term target of 61.00. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 16, 2015 02:36 ET (07:36 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150116eb1g000jd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
