\par\par \b \uc2 Rupee Stronger but Needs to Cross 61.68 to Solidify Gains -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2015\par 06:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0539 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/INR is lower than its Thursday close of 62.06, implying a stronger rupee versus the U.S. dollar, but speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keeping it from gaining too fast may be holding USD/INR back for now. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday--after cutting its repo rate to make it cheaper for banks to borrow money--to quell the rupee's 1.0% gain, says an offshore trader. The RBI could still be lurking around, supporting the bids in USD/INR around its current level of 61.92. If, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps away and USD/INR closes Friday below the 61.68 floor of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone, a bearish-dollar technical signal will be activated. Chart-motivated traders could then be encouraged to short the dollar versus the rupee for a near-term target of 61.00. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0540 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Insurers are sharply lower after the yield on the benchmark 10-year Japanese Government Bond (JGB) dropped to 0.235% on Friday--a fresh record low. Rates for 20-year JGBs hit 0.895%, while the 30s hit 1.08%--both the lowest since the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  introduced quantitative and qualitative easing in April 2013. Dai-Ichi Life (8750.TO) is down 4.1% at Y1,547, and \uc2 T&D Holdings\uc2  (8795.TO) is off 2.3% at Y1,282. "Cheap crude prices will keep inflation down and kill profits for life insurers, which typically have huge stocks of JGBs in their investment portfolios," says Norihiro Fujito, senior investment strategist at Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities. "Oil is the main inflation driver globally. But it may take months to years before the crude market turns around." Yields on 5-year JGBs remain at 0.0%, which they hit for the first time Tuesday.(bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0536 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Record-high electricity consumption in December in China was likely the effect of seasonal factors--heating at the onset of winter and factories restarting after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation\f28 \uc2 \f2  summit in November--rather than an outright demand recovery, analysts say. China said Friday it consumed a record 511.7 billion kilowatt-hours in December, up 4.7% from a year earlier. "The question is the growth--it's the most important indicator and it's in line with figures that show the economy is still slowing," said investment bank North Square Blue Oak's Miao Tian. The pace of growth just matches levels in the first half of this year, when growth was still relatively anemic. (chuin-wei.yap@wsj.com; Twitter @YapCW) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0529 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is less worried about high household debt in 2015 after its growth has appeared to be slowing down in recent months. "The household debt problem is not worrying because consumption-related loans [now] account for 3 in 10 of total loans," says Tongurai Limpiti, a deputy governor at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Outstanding consumer loans currently stand at 3.44 trillion baht [$105 billion], compared with outstanding loans of 11.08 trillion baht [$339 billion]." The central reported earlier that Thailand's household debt was 83.5% of gross domestic product in the second quarter of 2014. Tongurai also notes that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not expect non-performing loans to rise considerably in the first quarter of this year after its ratio was at 2.34% in third quarter 2014, compared with 2.15% for 2014. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0510 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Oil markets are feeling some of the impact after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  removed its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cap against the euro, analyst Daniel Ang at Singapore's Phillip Futures says. He says the U.S. dollar index has soared and the euro weakened, weighing on oil prices. "We previously identified the bottom for crude prices to be at $46 for Brent and $43 for west Texas intermediate. Prices are indeed showing heavy support here suggesting that we could be the bottom already," he adds. "All our forecasts seem to point towards a consolidation stage in the weeks to come," Ang says, adding that crude prices may stay rangebound. February \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nymex\f28 \uc2 \f2  crude is up $0.32 at $46.57 a barrel, March Brent crude rose $0.32 to $48.59 a barrel. (eric.yep@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0500 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kaisa Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (1638.HK) problems with blocked apartments, which appeared to have spread to a second Chinese city, underscore a feature of the Chinese property market: Many developers sell apartments before they are completed. That gives developers needed cash to complete projects. But accounts of angry Kaisa homeowners seeking answers to the fate of their apartments could give future buyers at other projects pause. This also highlights the urgency for property developers to seek alternative funding for the construction of homes. A real-estate portal in Hangzhou says more than 700 apartments at a Kaisa development there have been frozen. It already faces blocked apartments in Shenzhen. (esther.fung@wsj.com; Twitter: @estherfung) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0419 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Chinese stocks were higher at the lunchtime break, with the Shanghai Composite last up 1% at 3371.23, as the index was on track for its tenth consecutive weekly gain--its longest winning streak since 2007. The market remained buoyant following Thursday's lending data. Loan growth is slowing in China but total social financing--which encompasses shadow banking credit--picked up. The total social financing number from yesterday "is certainly helping," says David Welch, head of equity sales trading at Reorient Group. "But the number speaks to a broader issue in that China has room for more monetary easing," he said. The Shenzhen Composite adds 0.9% to 1473.42. (Daniel.Inman@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0415 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indian shares opened lower Friday, tracking weak cues from regional markets and also due to profit-booking after Thursday's sharp rise. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  BSE Sensex was down 0.4% at 27977.64, while the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Nifty index fell 0.4% to 8463.60. The benchmark Sensex index jumped 2.7% on Thursday following a surprise rate cut by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Analysts said investors will now watch the government's moves to speed up reforms. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Consultancy Services\f28 \uc2 \f2  (532540.BY) declined 1.7% after it posted only a 5% increase in its fiscal third-quarter profit. Other Sensex losers include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel\f28 \uc2 \f2  (532454.BY), \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Steel\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500470.BY), \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICICI Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  (532174.BY) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500112.BY). (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: FLS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0411 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Louis Cooper\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Managing Director of OANDA, an online retail \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading house, says the unexpected decision by SNB will continue to produce fallout in the markets over coming weeks as the "speed and ferocity" of the market movements have exposed undercapitalized participants. Cooper said \f28 \uc2 \f2 OANDA\f28 \uc2 \f2  itself experienced "significant losses" but is managing the "historic" situation". "We are a very well capitalized business. There are players that won't be." The shock to markets ranks among the biggest seen in recent years, and it has been amplified by the fact that the SNB had given no indication of change, and indeed, had affirmed its commitment to the cap only recently, Cooper added. "Some of these providers will not be able to maintain business as usual and even worse will be going out of business. I think this is the start of more news coming over the next few days," Cooper said. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0346 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's surprise move to decouple the franc from the euro has been one of the strongest hints to date that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to actively weaken the euro and embark on a bond-buying program at its January 22 meeting, says Ben Alexander, who is overseeing a fixed-interest portfolio of A$5.6 billion at Ardea Investment Management in Sydney. "Europe is a mess", he says, predicting that Australian government debt will now become even more attractive to offshore buyers. A fresh proof of the strong demand came overnight, when the benchmark 10-year bond yield dropped to a new record low of 2.509%. (vera.sprothen@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0338 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's Finance Ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan Bank for International Cooperation\f28 \uc2 \f2  is offering to help the Vietnamese government raise funds selling yen-denominated bonds in Japan. The ministry said in a statement JBIC has introduced some Japanese advisers for the bond sales, including SMBC Nikko. No details on any planned bond sales are available. The ministry added that it is also encouraging Japanese investors to buy Vietnam's government dong-denominated bonds. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0336 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy volte-face on Thursday briefly interrupted a meeting of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Allianz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's chief investment officers, who immediately began discussing how to take advantage of the Swiss franc's move, says Andreas Utermann, global chief investment officer at AllianzGlobal Investors. He told colleagues he should short the franc to make a quick profit from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's action. "But by the time we got our heads around it, it had already recovered... so we said let's get on with our meeting," he said. "It took about 15 minutes, and that was an opportunity lost, but so what." Still, he said he profited from the Swiss franc's appreciation: "Unless you were short the Swiss franc against the euro, which probably very few people were, how would you lose money yesterday?" (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; Twitter @gregorhunter) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 16, 2015 00:40 ET (05:40 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150116eb1g000js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
