\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Heavy Under U.S. Bond Yield Pressure -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2015\par 02:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1895-6.1995    6.1658-6.2000 \par USD/TWD   31.760-31.920    31.600-32.000 \par USD/KRW    1,080-1,088      1,070-1,090 \par USD/SGD   1.3300-1.3358    1.3280-1.3400 \par USD/MYR   3.5670-3.6000    3.5280-3.6000 \par USD/THB    32.75-32.81      32.64-32.87 \par USD/PHP    44.62-44.76      44.59-44.92 \par USD/IDR   12,530-12,630    12,430-12,740 \par USD/INR    62.00-62.54      61.56-63.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--downtrend. Spot USD/CNY has taken on a bearish technical bias after it closed below 6.1995 on Wednesday thus activating the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. The U.S. dollar index subsided overnight on falling government bond yields and lower retail sales data, which ought to influence the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  to shift the daily USD/CNY benchmark rate lower from Wednesday's 6.1205. A lower daily benchmark rate will weigh spot USD/CNY toward the daily Ichimoku Cloud support at 6.1658. The overnight fall of copper prices has taken over the spotlight from crude oil's recent collapse; markets are blaming China - the world's biggest consumer of the base metal - as part of the reason for the drop in prices. The slowdown in demand from China is a reminder that the government is shifting away from manufacturing-led economic growth and attempting to build a more consumption-centric economy. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.1895 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1800 (psychological support), before 6.1658 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone). Immediate resistance is at 6.1995 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.2096 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation lower. USD/TWD may test the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 31.760 as regional lead indicator USD/JPY fell overnight on weaker U.S. retail sales data - which led to lower \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bond yields. USD/TWD could take on a bearish chart bias if it closes Thursday below the 31.600 entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. The price difference between the benchmark 1-month USD/TWD contract and that of the spot contract may fall back under par - from its current premium of 0.015 - as U.S. dollar weakness spreads. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.760 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 31.600 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 31.500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 31.920 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 32.080 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--downtrend. USD/KRW opens with a well-bid tone Thursday - despite overnight U.S. dollar weakness - as traders speculate that \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  could cut interest rates. The BOK monetary policy decision due at 0100 GMT could weaken the won if a dovish stance is adopted. Since late last year, analysts have been suggesting that the BOK could cut rates to stimulate growth - an argument more pertinent now that the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  has lowered global growth expectations for 2015. USD/KRW is however still in the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that caps at 1,088. A Thursday close above this barrier would negate the bearish technical bias and open the way to the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance line at 1,096. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,080 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support and round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,070 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,068 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 1,088 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,090 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,096 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD has been flitting in and out of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel but may consolidate lower as the continued drop in U.S government bond yields makes it less attractive to hold the U.S. dollar. The overnight fall of USD/JPY - a lead indicator for the region - is also a factor that may prevent USD/SGD from entering the Bollinger uptrend channel. The yield on the benchmark U.S. 10-year government bond has fallen to around 1.84% after weaker-than-expected U.S. retail sales data. Sustained demand for safe-haven bonds has been depressing the yield on U.S. Treasurys. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.3300 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.3280 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1.3214 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.3358 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.3400 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.3412 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--uptrend. USD/MYR has retreated sharply from Wednesday's 5.5-year high of 3.6020 as crude oil prices rebounded strongly overnight. But the daily Bollinger uptrend channel remains in effect - contingent on a Thursday close above 3.5670 - which could keep USD/MYR buoyant. Oil prices got a reprieve as focus shifted to copper - which fell substantially on Wednesday. But bearish forecasts for oil by global investment banks as well as oil producer Saudi Arabia are unlikely to be brushed off in the near term. The persistent weakness of oil prices has been hurting investor sentiment for the ringgit because Malaysia's trade balance - as an oil producer and exporter - will be adversely affected. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.5670 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.5280 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.6000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 3.6070 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.6200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--mild downtrend. USD/THB has a mild bearish bias that could lead to 32.64 in the near term. The pair entered the Bollinger downtrend channel on Tuesday but is also caught inside the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone that spans 32.64-32.91. A break of the Cloud's base at 32.64 is necessary to trigger more U.S. dollar downside. The yield on the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury note fell further overnight to hit a 1.5-year low of 1.80%, due to demand for bonds from haven-seeking investors after weak U.S. retail sales data, hence depressing the greenback in general. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.75 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 32.64 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 32.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.81 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 32.87 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 32.91 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation lower. USD/PHP may break the base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 44.62 and drop into the Bollinger downtrend channel at 44.59 as appeal for the U.S. dollar wanes due to falling yields on \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bonds. The greenback is under pressure after U.S. retail sales data disappointed on Wednesday. The overnight fall of stocks - partly due to the connotations of copper prices collapsing - sent investors into safe-haven assets thus depressing bond yields. But a factor that could thwart U.S. dollar bears is a further fall of the euro - on expectations of quantitative easing by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.62 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone), then at 44.59 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.43 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.76 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 44.92 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.96 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation lower. USD/IDR may subside toward the nearby 20-day Bollinger mid support at 12,530 and then settle. The greenback retreated broadly overnight due to weak \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bond yields triggered by a flight to safety by investors on falling stocks and disappointing retail sales data. But the impending monetary policy decision by \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  - due at 0630 GMT - could provide a catalyst for the rupiah. The street expects little change in tone from the Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - especially since inflation is less of a threat given low commodity prices - but if BI sounds a cautious tone about growth prospects, the rupiah could react positively on expectations for easier monetary policy to come. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,530 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 12,500 (psychological support), before 12,430 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 12,630 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,740 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,970 (top of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 14 Jan 2015 20:05 ET  USD/Asia Heavy Under U.S. Bond Yield Pressure -- -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation lower. An overnight drop in the benchmark U.S. dollar index could drag USD/INR down to the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 61.87. The possibility of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  near that level to prevent excessive rupee strength - as they were suspected to have done on Tuesday - could augment the chart barrier. But if USD/INR falls through the Cloud support zone - which bottoms out at 61.56 - there is likely to be more rupee appreciation versus the dollar in the near term. The market has recently turned bullish for the rupee after a couple of notable global investment banks highlighted similar trading ideas last week. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.00 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and round-figure trading barrier), then at 61.87 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 61.56 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone), before 61.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.54 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 63.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 63.07 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 14, 2015 20:05 ET (01:05 GMT)\par \par \