\par\par \b \uc2 India Starts Rolling out \uc2 National Broadband Network\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2015\par 05:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0439 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Indian government has started rolling out a national broadband network from the southern state of Kerala. The network is aimed at taking government and individual services directly to citizens with the help of broadband. The network will also be used by telecom companies for providing internet services, and television cable companies. Through this network, India aims to cut transaction and traveling costs of citizens, which would boost economic growth. (krishna.jai@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @jaikrishna) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "AUD/JPY May Fall to 94 on Oil Price Tumble -- Market Talk," at 0322 GMT, misstated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair in the last line. The correct description is the AUD/USD, not the USD/AUD.\par \par \uc2 0343 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  said it has allowed \uc2 Vietnam Joint Stock Commercial Bank for Industry and Trade\uc2  (CTG.VH), or \uc2 VietinBank\uc2 , to open a wholly-owned unit in Laos. The unit, \uc2 VietinBank\uc2  Laos, will have a registered capital of $50 million and will be located in Vientiane, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. It said the unit is to be up and running within the next two years.(trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @TrongKhanhVu) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0343 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says a debt restructuring for the struggling Kaisa (1638.HK) is likely in the cards as more creditors are asking for the local courts to preserve assets, and all of the real-estate company's Shenzhen assets are still locked by the government. Kaisa's bonds are hovering at around 40-48 cents on a dollar, slightly down from 44-49 cents Tuesday, after jumping from 30-37 cents Monday after Kaisa said it was looking to appoint a financial adviser. Deutsche says having a financial adviser signals "a starting point for a potential debt restructuring," which may be "the start of a lengthy and painful process for bondholders." And there are still lots of questions lingering: could the firm pay even if investors accept a substantial haircut on the bonds? Who will step in and pay the bill? Can it transfer money offshore to foreign funds? DB recommends selling Kaisa's bonds, estimating their fair value at 33-38 cents. (fiona.law@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0331 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  will announce the lowest accepted price for newly auctioned 30-year Japanese government bonds at 0345 GMT, with traders saying it will likely come in around 108.30. The latest issue reopens the existing No. 45 issue, which carries a coupon of 1.5%. With government bonds rallying across the globe on concerns over falling oil prices, there are expectations that the auction will attract solid demand, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokai Tokyo Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief bond strategist Kazuhiko Sano. Lead JGB futures are up 0.03 at 148.32. (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0330 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Nikkei is down 1.1% at 16901.20 midday as the dollar slips further, now at Y117.43. "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's cut of its global economic growth forecasts (to +2.6% for the global economy in 2014 and to +3% in 2015) is having an effect on sentiment, particularly from a commodity price perspective," says an equity trading director at a European brokerage. "Falls in oil, iron ore, copper, and nickel, etc. are filtering through to stock prices." He notes that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been fervent in its market support, having bought some Y34 billion in exchange-traded funds (ETFs) Tuesday alone. "No doubt stocks would be much lower this week without \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  support," he says. (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0328 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China yuan extends Tuesday's gains after the country posted stronger-than-expected trade data in December. The yuan is at 6.1954 versus 6.1983 late Tuesday. The market shrugs off the daily fixing set by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is at 6.1205 versus 6.1195 Tuesday. "The market is turning more bullish about the yuan after it broke the 6.2000 key psychological level yesterday," says a Shanghai-based foreign bank trader. Offshore, one-year USD/CNY non-deliverable forwards are down at 6.2925 from 6.3055 late Tuesday. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0326 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Chinese developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kaisa Group Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' (1638.HK) default on a payment on an offshore bond raises costs for other developers looking to raise debt and it will take time for the dust to settle, says Jefferies analysts in a note. Many creditors have sought immediate loan repayment and for the court to freeze Kaisa's assets, while project partners have demanded refunds. "Until market confidence is restored, it would distort the timetable when developers can submit applications for debt issues, as we expect that, no matter the regulatory body or investor, the vetting process will be more stringent than usual." Developers heavily reliant on offshore funding, such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agile Property Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  (3383.HK), \f28 \uc2 \f2 Evergrande Real Estate Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (3333.HK), \f28 \uc2 \f2 Country Garden Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  (2007.HK) and KWG Property Holding (1813.HK) will be more vulnerable to the restrained offshore financing channel, Jefferies adds. (esther.fung@wsj.com, @estherfung) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0322 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Already facing selling pressure on tumbling oil prices, the AUD/JPY may fall to 94 later this week, says Yasuaki Amatatsu, analyst of global markets research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\f28 \uc2 \f2  UFJ. The ongoing decline in oil prices and those on natural resources suggest fallloff in Australia's exports, prompting some of investors to sell the commodity-linked AUD, says Amatatsu. The AUD/JPY falls to as low as 95.13, its lowest since Oct. 28, before recovering slightly to 95.24 now. The AUD/USD also down to a week low of 0.8098 and now at 0.8108. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corrections and Amplifications\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This item was corrected at 04:19 GMT. The original misstated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair in the last line. The correct description is the AUD/USD, not the USD/AUD.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0316 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Record-high commodity imports to China last month and last year likely reflected not just low prices but a strategic wish to stock pile, Capital Economics said. "It seems unlikely that opportunistic buying is the whole story. Buyers are unlikely to build stocks unless they are confident of future demand," the research house says. Capital expects commodity import demand to remain strong in the first quarter of 2015 as lower prices continue to encourage some additional buying. "Meanwhile, copper demand will be supported by a pick-up in investment by the State Grid and by attractive charges at smelters," Capital analyst \f28 \uc2 \f2 Caroline Bain\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. (chuin-wei.yap@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @YapCW) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0303 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/INR is likely to test the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 61.87--and possibly the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's resolve--as the U.S. dollar settles lower in Asia Wednesday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot market this week to temper the rapid rise of the rupee. Traders have been betting aggressively on the rupee against the dollar after a couple of notable global investment banks highlighted bullish rupee trading ideas last week. The decline of oil prices may also be a factor helping the rupee. Cheaper oil means cheaper imported energy bills and thereby a reduced trade deficit for India. USD/INR is expected to open around 62.03, based on its overnight offshore market closing, versus its Tuesday close of 61.97. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0238 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/THB has a mild bearish bias that could lead to 32.64 in the near term--implying a stronger baht versus the U.S. dollar. The pair entered the Bollinger downtrend channel on Tuesday but is also caught inside the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone that spans 32.64-32.91, suggesting the move lower could be protracted. A break of the Cloud's base at 32.64 is necessary to trigger more U.S. dollar downside. The yield on the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury note has remained under 2.00%, due to demand for bonds from haven-seeking investors, depressing the greenback in general. USD/THB is now 32.81 from its Tuesday close of 32.80. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 13, 2015 23:39 ET (04:39 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150114eb1e000k0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
