\par\par \b \uc2 India Imported Crude Oil Price Falls Again -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2015\par 08:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0712 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India's oil ministry said the price of its imported crude-oil basket fell to $45.86 a barrel Monday from $47.36 Friday, reflecting volatility in global crude prices. Oil prices fell for the second consecutive day with both the crude benchmarks down nearly 2% in Asian trade Tuesday. Oil prices had lost around 5% on Monday alone, extending the selloff that has gripped oil markets since mid-2014, as sell-side analysts slashed price forecasts and warned of a prolonged glut in global oil markets that will extend well into 2015. Markets have been fumbling around for a price floor, especially after the \uc2 Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  decided not to cut output to stem the decline in prices. A fall in crude-oil prices is positive for India's economy as the country imports three-quarters of its energy needs. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @journosaurabh) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0700 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Oil prices sunk Tuesday with the U.S. oil benchmark dropping below $45 a barrel after United Arab Emirates' oil minister said the \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  won't adjust output, and that other producers need to be rational. He says oil prices could take two or three years to stabilize and \uc2 OPEC\uc2  is concerned about the oil-market balance, but that it can't be the only party responsible for balancing the market. The UAE is one of the 10 largest oil and natural gas producers in the world, and a member of \uc2 OPEC\uc2 . \uc2 Nymex\uc2  west Texas intermediate crude is down $1.08 at $44.99/barrel, Brent crude is down $1.28 at $46.15/barrel. (eric.yep@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0618 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The latest rebound in India's industrial output was primarily due to distortions caused by the change in timing of the Diwali festival this year, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Adjusted for those effects, an industrial recovery still appears feeble, which, coupled with a better-than-expected inflation print, reinforces the case for rate cuts by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "Looking past these statistical quirks shows that the growth momentum in manufacturing is still weak," \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. "We expect 50 basis points in rate cuts in 2015," it adds. India's industrial output rose 3.8% from a year earlier in November, after a 4.2% contraction the previous month. Meanwhile, the consumer inflation rate climbed to 5% in December from 4.38% in November, but was still better than the 5.40% prediction of economists. (anant.kala@wsj.com; @anantvkala) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0601 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY is gaining momentum to as high as Y118.70 with short-covering pushing up the pair, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  senior vice president Toshiyuki Umekawa, adding that options-related stop-loss buying orders just above Y118.50 are giving the pair an extra lift. The pair is now at Y118.66, but "we still lack cues to bring the pair much higher." But Mr. Umekawa says the pair has managed to confirm Y118 as the lower end of its trading range for now. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PAB \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0601 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Taiwan shares finish 0.6% higher at 9231.80, as gains in airline and petrochemical stocks offset declines in most tech heavyweights. Mega Securities analyst \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alex Huang\f28 \uc2 \f2  says investors predict limited downside for oil prices from currently low levels and several petrochemical and textile stocks have sunk to attractive prices. China Man-Made Fiber (1718.TW) closes limit-up 6.7% at NT$11.90 and China Petrochemical (1314.TW) rises 3.4% to NT$12.25. Airlines, naturally, rise on tumbling oil prices: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eva Airways\f28 \uc2 \f2  (2618.TW) gains 1.9% to NT$24.65 and \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Airlines\f28 \uc2 \f2  (2610.TW) ends up 3.2% at NT$16.30. Tech stocks are mostly lower, as 1Q is the sector's traditionally low season. \f28 \uc2 \f2 MediaTek\f28 \uc2 \f2  (2454.TW) falls 1.0% to NT$483.00 and HTC (2498.TW) ends down 3.0% at NT$147.50. TSMC (2330.TW) bucks the downtrend and gains 0.4% to NT$132.50 ahead of its 4Q earnings release Thursday. (aries.poon@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0558 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] After chalking up a gain of 2.4% versus the U.S. dollar over the past four days, India's rupee is pulling back slightly and now trades a tad weaker at 62.13 versus its Monday close of 62.07. USD/INR is firming up ahead of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support at 61.87 as traders take profit on short-USD bets placed last week when a couple of notable global investment banks suggested the rupee would appreciate in the near term. Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday at current levels--an attempt to dampen rupee volatility--may have created a temporary floor for USD/INR and prompted speculators to reduce their short-USD/INR bets, says an offshore trader. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0539 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The recently convened Indonesian House of Representatives is likely to accomplish two tasks over the next two weeks, according to Eurasia Group. The first is approving President Joko Widodo's revised state budget, which reallocates some $17.3 billion saved from curtailing fuel subsidies for use in infrastructure and social development projects. Second, parliament will likely act to reinstate direct elections of hundreds of regional leaders such as governors and mayors. Lawmakers in September passed a bill ending such elections. Other issues--such as the possibility of new regulations for the banking and oil industries--will be put aside until various political parties determine their leadership, Eurasia Group reckons. (newley.purnell@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @Newley) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0529 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The yen is retreating from a near-four-week high of 117.74 against the U.S. dollar Tuesday as risk appetite improves following healthier-than-expected China December trade data, while Tokyo stocks pared morning losses. Japan's Nikkei Stock Average was recently down 1.45% at 16,948 after recovering more than 100 points from its morning low of 16,828. Meanwhile, U.S. stock index futures are now trading in positive territory. Further upside in USD/JPY may encounter resistance at 118.68, then at 119.32. Spot USD/JPY is at 118.33. (jerry.tan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0527 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The South Korea won could rise sharply versus the U.S. dollar in the near term if a key USD/KRW chart support is broken by Tuesday's close. A confirmed break of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone--contingent on a daily close below 1,079--might trigger liquidation of long-USD positions. The break of the cloud base is a bearish technical signal that might accelerate the U.S. dollar's slide. Below the cloud support, the next clear technical floor is the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 1,068 followed by the weekly Bollinger mid-line at 1,052. The greenback has been falling against the won for four days as the yield on the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury note remains under pressure below 2.00%. A low yield on \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds intrinsically makes the dollar less attractive to hold as an investment. USD/KRW is now 1,080.5 from its Monday close of 1,081.4. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0519 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Sri Lanka last week surprised everyone by electing a new president, but \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  cannot tell if this will result in an improved sovereign rating for the country. President Maithripala Sirisena inherits an economy that has been growing fast, partly because of investment and construction projects undertaken after the civil war ended in 2009, but also one that is heavily indebted. In 2013, government debt stood at 78% of gross domestic product. The median government debt of other comparable countries stood at 41%, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . A large chunk of Sri Lankan's government's debt is denominated in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "Whether the political transition has meaningful sovereign credit implications will depend on the fiscal and investment policies Sirisena's administration pursues," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (shefali.anand@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0507 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/IDR is stable near its Monday closing level of 12,595 after an initial pop in the safe haven U.S. dollar early Tuesday when risk aversion seemed to be the theme of the day. But the impressive rise in China's December exports has lifted general investor sentiment and buffered regional stock markets from the 0.8% decline seen in U.S. stocks overnight. Risk-sensitive emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Indonesia rupiah are hence recovering from mild weakness. The daily USD/IDR chart suggests a consolidation pattern may hold unless the 12,430-12,640 range breaks. Tuesday's 9.7% rise in China's exports for December, which trumped forecasts for a much smaller gain of 6.6%, has helped the Indonesia stock exchange index rally 0.3%. USD/IDR is now 12,600 from its Monday close of 12,595. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: AAP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0505 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's milder-than-anticipated December rise in consumer prices was crucial, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kotak Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Kotak says the data showed Indian inflation is getting tamer, paving the way for a rate cut from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in February. The broker expects there is a room for 1% rate cut by end the of 2015. Late Monday, India reported a milder-than-anticipated rise in inflation. The consumer inflation rate climbed to 5% in December from 4.38% in November, but it was below the analysts' prediction of 5.40% and is still well below the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's target of 8% for January. "We now estimate the January-March 2015 inflation to average around 5.7%," Kotak says. (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 13, 2015 02:12 ET (07:12 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150113eb1d000sr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
