\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Indian markets off lows, foreign investors in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2014\par 12:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends at 63.615/625 per dlr, off 13-mth low\par \par \uc2 * NSE trims losses, ends down 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2 * 10-yr bond yield ends down 2 bps at 7.97 pct (Updates closing levels for rupee, debt)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 17 (Reuters) - The rupee retreated from 13-month lows after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while bonds also recovered despite concerns over whether foreign funds will stick with India, one of the star performers this year among emerging markets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was larger than in recent sessions, traders said, with some estimating dollar sales of nearly $500 million. Meanwhile, buying of shares by state-run \uc2 Life Insurance Corporation of India\uc2  helped shares recover from earlier falls to trade flat, dealers added.\par \par \uc2 Analysts fear more foreign selling, but doubt it would spark turmoil anywhere similar to last year when India suffered its worst market crisis since 1991.\par \par \uc2 Unlike then, India is now seen as benefitting from sharp falls in inflation, hefty \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, and a less troublesome current account gap.\par \par \uc2 "We are less worried as overall market conditions are better, like fiscal condition is within control, current account deficit is low, inflation is falling," a senior policymaker aware of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking told Reuters, declining to be identified discussing the country's exchange rate policy.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 63.6150/6250 per dollar, weaker than its 63.53/54 close. It had earlier weakened to as much as 63.89, its lowest since Nov. 13, 2013.\par \par \uc2 The rupee's initial weakness came after foreign funds sold shares worth $196.56 million on Tuesday, their biggest daily net sales since Oct. 17, and a sixth consecutive day of selling.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors also turned sellers of debt for the first time in December on Monday, having sold a net $146.56 million.\par \par \uc2 But analysts say India is better placed to withstand foreign selling, given the current account deficit has narrowed to 2.1 percent of gross domestic product from a record high of 4.8 percent in the fiscal year ended in March 2013.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $314.66 billion as of Friday, not far from the record high of $320.785 billion in September 2011.\par \par \uc2 India has attracted a combined $43.2 billion in foreign flows into debt and shares so far this year. As a result, the NSE index is still up around 25 percent in 2014, the second-best performer in Asia in dollar terms.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 10-year bond yield hit a session high of 8.03 percent, its highest since Dec. 1, before retreating to end the day down 2 basis points at 7.97 percent. The yield is still up 14 bps for the week. (Editing by Rafael Nam, Sunil Nair and \uc2 Jacqueline Wong\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-17T12:42:12.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141217each006mz\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Sensex Extends Recent Losses On Global Cues\b0\par\par\uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2014\par \uc2 RTT News\par \uc2 RTTNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2014 NoticiasFinancieras. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (RTTNews) - Indian shares extended recent losses on Wednesday, but the benchmark indexes ended well off their day's lows, aided by buying of shares by state-run \uc2 Life Insurance Corporation of India\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investor sentiment remained muted amid weak global cues, as a rout in oil prices continued and fears intensified that some of Russia's largest companies could default on their dollar-denominated debts.\par \par \uc2 Russia's embattled ruble recovered against the U.S. dollar and euro today after the Russian Finance unveiled plans to start selling its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings, saying the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "extremely undervalued".\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee also recovered from a fresh 13-month low against the dollar on suspended \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is still not an alarming situation as fiscal condition is within control, current account deficit is low and inflation falling, media reports quoted a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official as saying.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brent crude futures fell more than a percent to trade near a 5-1/2 year low under $60 a barrel in Asian deals, reinforcing expectations inflation will remain low or continue to fall in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark \uc2 S&P\uc2  BSE Sensex fell more than a percent in early trading before recouping most of its loss to end the session down 71.31 points or 0.27 percent at 26,710.13. The broader CNX Nifty index also cut early loss to close down 37.80 points or 0.47 percent at 8,029.80.\par \par \uc2 Among the prominent decliners, Cipla, \uc2 Sun Pharma\uc2 , \uc2 Hero MotoCorp\uc2 , \uc2 ITC\uc2 , \uc2 Bharti Airtel\uc2 , \uc2 Cairn India\uc2 , \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2 , Lupin, DLF and \uc2 Asian Paints\uc2  fell 2-4 percent.\par \par \uc2 Mahindra & Mahindra\uc2  dropped 1.2 percent. The auto major said it will observe up to seven "no production days" a month at some of its plants till March 2015. \uc2 Tata Power Company\uc2  dropped 1.8 percent after commissioning a wind farm in Maharashtra.\par \par \uc2 SpiceJet\uc2  shares slumped 5.4 percent. The cash-strapped airline was forced to ground its entire fleet after oil companies refused to provide jet fuel to the company due to non-payment of dues.\par \par \uc2 Jewelry makers Titan Company and Thangamayil Jewelry fell 1-3 percent. The government on Tuesday raised import tariff value on gold to $396 per 10 grams and on silver to $561 per kg in line with volatile global price trends.\par \par \uc2 Jagran Prakashan\uc2  shares tumbled 5.4 percent. The company forayed into the radio segment with the acquisition of \uc2 Music Broadcast Private Limited\uc2 , which operates Radio City FM stations.\par \par \uc2 Metal stocks rebounded from Tuesday's losses, with \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2  gaining a percent after the Odisha government allowed the company to resume production from its four iron ore mines in the state in view of the High Court order. Hindalco advanced 1.8 percent and \uc2 Sesa Sterlite\uc2  rallied 3.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 State-run oil explorer ONGC rose 2.2 percent and lender SBI added 2.1 percent. \uc2 Jaiprakash Associates\uc2  soared 4.2 percent on bargain hunting after recent sharp losses.\par \par \uc2 On the global front, the Asian markets reversed early declines to end mostly higher, although the gains remained capped ahead of a \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  policy meeting. With a rout in oil prices accelerating and Russia's economic woes multiplying, there are expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will maintain its dovish policy stance on rates at the end of a two-day meeting later tonight.\par \par \uc2 European stocks drifted lower in early trading as investors took some profits off the table after sharp gains the previous day.\par \par \uc2 For comments and feedback: contact editorial@rttnews.com\par \par \uc2 Copyright(c) 2014 RTTNews.com. All Rights Reserved\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTTNEW0020141217each0040i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
