\par\par \b \uc2 India-Bangladesh Oil Pipeline Aimed at Boosting National Ties -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2014\par 09:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0824 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India is seeking cooperation from Bangladesh to build an oil pipeline between the two countries, its petroleum and natural gas minister Dharmendra Pradhan says. He met on Wednesday Tawfiq-e-Elahi Chowdhury, the energy adviser to the Prime Minister of Bangladesh, and discussed the need to greatly enhance cooperation in the oil and gas sector to the mutual benefit of both countries. Bangladesh helped India recently in the construction and generation of electricity from a power project in the eastern state of Tripura. The proposed pipeline project is part of a wider Indian program to strengthen ties between the two countries. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; Twitter: @journosaurabh) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 0759 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\uc2 Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to leave its main interest rate at 1.5% Thursday, which should offer support to the NOK. "Considering that the market is pricing a 50/50 chance of \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  cutting rates today, we expect large market moves," SEB bank says in a note. SEB's expectations would imply slightly higher short rates and lower EUR/NOK, they add. \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  sounds a note of caution, saying the NOK support could be short lived as the oil price is in free fall. Norway relies heavily on the oil industry. EUR/NOK trades at 8.9150. (charles.duxbury@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0757 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Yet another choppy overnight session for the U.S. dollar, with falling U.S. yields taking their toll. USD/JPY fell to a fresh two-week low as the Nikkei shed 2%, although the former made a limited recovery as the index ended the day 0.9% lower. Elsewhere the Kiwi dollar outperformed after the RBNZ left rates on hold as expected but retained a tightening bias which caught some in the market by surprise. Up ahead the SNB and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  are expected to keep rates on hold and the ECB will announces the take-up of the second round of its TLTRO program. Already out, German final November CPI came in as expected, flat on the month and +0.6% on the year, while French CPI was lower than expected, at -0.2% on the month and +0.3% on the year vs -0.1% and +0.4% forecast. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0754 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] With Thailand's disappointing economic growth recovery to-date, despite various short-term stimulus measures from the military-appointed government, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Nalin Chutchotitham suggests more fiscal spending may be needed to get the country back on track. "It has also been discouraging that the economy has not yet shown any signs of responding," says Nalin, who points out that the country still has plenty of headroom against the self-imposed long-term debt limit of 60% of GDP. "What may be needed at this stage is a shot in the arm for the economy to tide things over until big infrastructure projects get under way and private spending recovers as well." (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0751 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Wearable devices--which incorporate computer or electronic technology into products such as watches and glasses--will be increasingly difficult to distinguish from traditional products, Gartner says. The research firm reckons that by 2017 some 30% of such devices will be "completely unobtrusive to the eye," in fact. For example, smart contact lenses are being developed, as are smart items of jewelry that contain sensors providing emergency alerts. Even many smart glasses will become indistinguishable from traditional spectacles, Gartner says. (newley.purnell@wsj.com; Twitter: @Newley) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0749 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] All is not well in Malaysia's opposition coalition, Pakatan Rakyat, according to Lim Kit Siang, adviser to the Democratic Action Party (DAP), one of the three parties in the coalition. "If you ask me whether I can categorically say that the tripartite Pakatan Rakyat will be around to fight the 14GE [14th general election, due in 2018], I cannot answer you as I do not know," says Lim. But one political analyst believes it will be intact for the next general election. "It will depend extremely on PAS [Pan-Malaysian Islamic Party] president Hadi Awang. If he is removed or sidelined then it will be good for Pakatan Rakyat," says James Chin, a professor at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Monash University\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Kuala Lumpur campus. The coalition is made up of the People's Justice Party, led by opposition leader \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anwar Ibrahim\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the DAP and the PAS. "Hadi does not like Anwar and thinks the secular DAP is getting too strong in Pakatan Rakyat," said Chin. The ruling National Front party won the 2013 national elections but lost the popular vote (celine.fernandez@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0743 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The delicate process of bringing peace to the southern Philippine island of Mindanao is being threatened by a long-running refugee crisis in the city of Zamboanga, aid workers have warned. While a landmark peace deal signed earlier this year may yet end a conflict that has killed over 100,000 people since the 1970s, and open up resource-rich Mindanao to foreign investors, the plight of thousands of Muslim refugees--made homeless after Islamist militants attacked Zamboanga in September 2013--could derail the peace process unless the refugees' situation is improved soon. Aid workers, speaking privately, warned that Mindanao's Muslims would lose confidence in the government's promises of a new autonomous region if they felt that fellow Muslims in Zamboanga, already homeless for 15 months, were being neglected or victimized.(trefor.moss@wsj.com; Twitter @Trefor1) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0742 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The allotment of the second Targeted Long Term Refinancing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (1015 GMT) will be closely watched as the ECB looks to expand its balance sheet. Analysts at RBC expect the take-up to exceed the EUR82.6bn seen under the first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and expect a take-up around EUR120bn, at the low-end of the market's expectations. "This reflects our view that low participation in the first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  goes beyond just its timing, with banks also citing an absence of funding constraints, concerns over market stigma and the perceived weakness of loan demand. As such, we see a risk that take-up disappoints once again." (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0728 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 's expected downgrade to its economic growth forecast in January points to another rate cut to a record low 1.75%, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Ronald Man. "We forecast the next move by \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be a 25 basis-point rate cut in the first quarter of 2015 in response to a weaker growth outlook," he says after BOK Governor Lee Ju-yeol tells a post-rate decision press conference that it is "difficult" to maintain its 3.9% growth forecast for 2015 citing various downside risks. He also says it is "inevitable to lower the inflation forecast" of 2.4% for 2015 given subdued consumer prices. The BOK is scheduled to revise its growth and inflation forecasts in January. On Thursday it kept its policy rate unchanged at 2% for a second consecutive month after its August and October rate cuts.(kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0726 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to leave its target range for the 3-month CHF libor at 0.0%-0.25%, 0830 GMT, and the EUR/CHF floor at 1.20. With the cross trading close to this level, and adding to imported disinflation, the statement should retain a dovish tone. Shortly afterwards (0900 GMT), \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to keep its main rate unchanged at 1.5%, although, with sharply falling oil prices and looser policy in Sweden, the market has started to price in rate cuts for 2015. So it wouldn't be a surprise if the rate profile pushed back rate hikes or even pencilled in a cut for next year. EUR/NOK currently 8.93, EUR/CHF 1.2035. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0704 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Europe's low inflation story continues. Germany's statistics office confirmed Thursday that annual inflation for Europe's largest economy hit its lowest figure since February 2010. Prices were only 0.6% higher on the year in national terms, while in European harmonized terms they grew by 0.5%. Both were unchanged on the month. Energy was again one of the key components. In national terms, these prices were down by 2.5% on the year. Remember, Germany is one of the eurozone's stronger economies. Its weak inflation makes it harder for its eurozone partners to compete against it without cutting prices and wages, thus threatening to bring Europe into deflation. Something the Eurotower is surely thinking about. (todd.buell@wsj.com) (@ToddBuell) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0652 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's rupee has slid to 62.25 against the U.S. dollar--a level last seen in February--as Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stumble across the board on a regionwide fall in stock markets. The daily USD/INR chart suggests a bullish technical bias for the dollar is emerging, though that may change if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steps in to quell the dollar's rise. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was said to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot market when the rupee fell to 62.22 in November, thus raising the possibility of similar action today. Stocks on India's main exchange, known as the Sensex, are down 1.0%. Risk aversion has been brewing in Asia Thursday after a significant drop in U.S. stock markets overnight triggered by collapsing oil prices. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 11, 2014 03:24 ET (08:24 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141211eacb0010h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
