\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Hits 10-Month Low,  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  May Be Lurking -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,726 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2014\par 07:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0652 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India's rupee has slid to 62.25 against the U.S. dollar--a level last seen in February--as Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stumble across the board on a regionwide fall in stock markets. The daily USD/INR chart suggests a bullish technical bias for the dollar is emerging, though that may change if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in to quell the dollar's rise. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market when the rupee fell to 62.22 in November, thus raising the possibility of similar action today. Stocks on India's main exchange, known as the Sensex, are down 1.0%. Risk aversion has been brewing in Asia Thursday after a significant drop in U.S. stock markets overnight triggered by collapsing oil prices. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0650 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Japanese utilities' oil consumption this winter is likely to fall by one-third from last year unless weather turn out to be extremely cold or hot, says \uc2 Yasushi Kimura\uc2 , chairman of the Petroleum Association of Japan. The expected demand fall is because some new gas and coal-fired capacity came online during the past year, which would encourage utilities to cut use of expensive oil, Kimura says. Despite a recent drop in prices, oil remains much more expensive than gas and coal for power generation. Ten Japanese regional utilities consumed 13.9 billion liters of oil for power generation in October-March last winter, or 87.4 million barrels, according to \uc2 the Federation of Electric Power Companies of Japan\uc2 . (mari.iwata@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0646 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Philippine President Benigno Aquino pushed through on Thursday his two-day trip to the Korean port city of Busan to attend the two-day Asean-South Korean meeting. Aquino had previously cancelled the visit to focus on the disaster response following for Typhoon Hagupit. Aquino said his change of mind follows an assessment of the damage caused by the typhoon--known locally as Ruby--isn't as extensive as initially feared and that government officials are effectively responding to the disaster. Latest data released by government showed Hagupit damaged around $71 million of crops and infrastructure and around 43,000 houses. The typhoon killed 11 and displaced over 2.7 million people. Those figures could still rise but they aren't likely to go near the 6,300 deaths and $12 billion economic damage caused by Haiyan last year. Aquino will be back in Manila on Friday. (cris.larano@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0643 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Typically this is the time in December for investors to close out positions ahead of the year-end book closing, but there may still be some good chances to buy the USD/JPY on dips if the current risk-off mood continues, says a senior bank dealer. "Many investors are going ahead with profit-taking especially after the pair stretched up" to just below 122 earlier this month (now at 118.29). But "I myself am sure to buy if the pair hits 115 or 116 this week," the dealer says, adding that technical charts show there is still more room for the pair to test the downside. However, given the strength of dip-buying by Japanese importers and individuals who were already willing to buy at today's lows (the pair hit a two-week low of 117.44), a further big slide is unlikely. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0638 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The growth of China's industrial production, a key measure of the pulse of the economy, probably slowed to 7.5% on-year in November from 7.7% in October, according to the median forecast of 16 economists in a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  survey. "Industrial production was dampened as tens of thousands of factories were closed during the \f28 \uc2 \f2 APEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  summit in Beijing at the beginning of November," says Jianguang Shen of Mizuho Securities. A recent cut in interest rates also suggests policymakers are concerned about the strength of the economy, he says. Meanwhile the growth of fixed-asset investment probably eased to 15.8% on-year in the January to November period, from 15.9% in the first 10 months of the year. But retail sales likely picked up to 11.6% growth in October from 11.5% the previous month, according to the same poll. The data are due to be released at 0530 GMT on Friday. (richard.silk@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0621 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Philippine government on Thursday approved a 12% reduction in the minimum fare for the jeepney--the most popular and cheapest mode of transportation in the country. The reduction was due mainly to the steady decline in global prices of oil products, particularly diesel, which is used to power jeepneys. Taxi and bus fares are also expected to come down. Lower oil and transport prices should further moderate inflation and provide the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas\f28 \uc2 \f2  latitude to raise interest rates. At Thursday's meeting, all 13 economists polled by The Wall Street Journal expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stay on hold; many pencilling the next adjustment to come in the second half of 2015.(cris.larano@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0601 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japanese buyers of crude oil will likely to keep Iranian crude imports in 2015 flat from this year, at around 200,000 barrels a day, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yasushi Kimura\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chairman of Petroleum Association of Japan, citing the suspension of talks between the West and Iran. "There is no reason to cut nor to increase, because they didn't reach any agreement," Kimura says. Next talks are scheduled to start six months later, therefore any change in Iranian crude import volume would take place after the next talks, he says. (Mari.iwata@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0513 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The significant decline in global oil prices may prompt Indonesia to partially roll back last month's more than 30% hike in subsidized fuel prices early next year, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "We think there will be a one-off decline in fuel prices e.g. by Rp1,000/liter or 12% possibly in late January or February. This may be followed by further cuts if oil prices stay at current levels," it says. Former President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono\f28 \uc2 \f2  three times partially rolled back fuel price hikes during his first-five year term. Citi adds a 12% cut in domestic fuel prices may partially reverse the impact from the November fuel price hike by around 0.4 percentage point. "However, as public transport tariffs are downward-sticky, we don't expect the second-round deflation impact to be material yet." Furthermore, the government may increase the administered price of liquefied petroleum gas next year, which may mitigate the impact of fuel price cut on inflation. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0511 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's industrial output in October likely rose 2.4% from a year earlier, according to the median estimate in a poll of 16 economists by The Wall Street Journal. That would be little changed from September's 2.5% expansion. Economists are banking on a double-digit expansion in coal and electricity output--according to data already released--to have boosted broader industrial performance. However, a decline in exports as well as automobile sales would weigh on production. "While the recovery is certainly underway, its pace continues to remain modest," says Rupa Rege Nitsure, chief economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Baroda\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Moreover, its sustainability depends critically on the continued efforts by the government to resolve the issues surrounding the stalled projects." The data is due at 1200 GMT Friday. (anant.kala@wsj.com; @anantvkala) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0506 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] If USD/INR stays above 62.00 by Thursday's close, the daily Bollinger uptrend channel will be affirmed and could lead the dollar higher against the rupee in the near term. The rupee, currently at 62.14 to the dollar, is nearly unchanged from its Wednesday close of 62.11. Investors may be grappling with the mixed implications of the collapse of crude oil prices--which is good for India's current account deficit but negative for global growth expectations. Generally, investors are still optimistic on India because Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been aggressively courting foreign investment and implementing domestic changes to boost economic growth. Thus the rupee could still fare better versus regional counterparts even if it slides against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0500 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's yuan is trading at 6.1707, not far from its Thursday opening level of 6.1700 even as stocks on the Shanghai composite index slip 0.6%. The yuan has gained slightly versus its Wednesday close of 6.1768 after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the daily benchmark rate stronger against the U.S. dollar for a fifth consecutive day. But the recovery of the yuan may be temporary. The daily spot USD/CNY chart indicates that a bullish-dollar technical bias will prevail as long as the Bollinger channel is kept intact by a Thursday close above 6.1643. Shanghai stocks have recouped from the selloff triggered by tightened loan collateral criteria but may remain capped due to recent tepid Chinese economic growth and inflation data. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0447 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] South Korean equities fall after \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  holds interest rates at 2.00% amid deteriorating macroeconomic data, resisting pressure to make a third rate cut this year at its final meeting of 2014. "Rising levels of household debt suggest further rate cuts by \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 ... are unlikely," says Capital Economics. "In fact, with GDP growth set to accelerate in the coming months, we think the next move in rates is more likely to be a hike than a cut, but probably not until the second half of next year." The KOSPI Index, the worst performing in Asia-Pacific this year, falls 1.3% to 1,920.84.(gregor.hunter@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2  @gregorhunter) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 11, 2014 01:52 ET (06:52 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141211eacb000vb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
