\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee sees biggest gain in 1-1/2 months as shares hit record\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2014\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends at 59.6875/6975 per dlr vs 60.07/08 on Tuesday               \par \par \uc2 * Heavy dollar selling by custodian banks, corporates aids               \par \par \uc2 * RBI steps in to buy dollars to prevent sharp rupee gains               \par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat               \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 2 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee posted on Wednesday its biggest single-day gain since mid-May and rose to its highest level in more than two weeks on the back of heavy dollar sales by custodian banks along with some corporate dollar inflows.               \par \par \uc2 Aiding sentiment was a record run by Indian shares after Finance Minister Arun Jaitley's warning against "mindless populism" raised hopes the government would unveil a fiscally prudent budget next week.               \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollars sporadically after the unit crossed 59.70 levels, but strong inflows helped the rupee continue to gain nonetheless. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tended to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rupee strengthens above 60 to the dollar.               \par \par \uc2 "Now that the psychological level of 60 has been breached and with a close of below 59.70, there could be potential further gains for the rupee. But RBI can step in to buy at any point," said Paresh Nayar, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income trading at First Rand Bank.               \par \par \uc2 "The budget is going to be the most keenly watched budget after many years. The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be impacted based on the outlook for inflows in various sectors based on specific measures taken."               \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed at 59.6875/6975 per dollar compared with 60.07/08 on Tuesday. The unit rose to 59.62, its strongest since June 13, while the day's low was 60.07.               \par \par \uc2 The movement in global crude, given the impact on inflation and the current account deficit, will be monitored. India imports nearly two-thirds of its oil needs.               \par \par \uc2 Oil fell towards $111 a barrel on Wednesday, its lowest in almost three weeks, on a possible substantial recovery in Libyan exports after rebels said they would reopen two oil terminals.               \par \par \uc2 In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 59.90, while the three-month was at 60.48.                              \par \par \uc2 FACTORS TO WATCH * Dlr stable after hitting lows, awaits Yellen, \uc2 ADP\uc2  data   * Won at 6-yr high despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  up   * Asia shares score 3-yr high on economic optimism    * Foreign institutional investor flows             * For data on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-2T12:55:02.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140702ea720076j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
