\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee ends weak as Iraq crisis worsens; RBI steps in to check fall\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2014\par 13:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends at 60.39/40 per dlr vs 60.03/04 on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 * RBI spotted selling dlrs around 60.53 rupee levels - traders\par \par \uc2 * Iraq-driven oil spike threatens to blow hole in Indian budget - sources\par \par \uc2 By Neha Dasgupta\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 18 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell on Wednesday as the worsening crisis in Iraq threatened to disrupt oil supplies but recovered from session lows after state-owned banks sold dollars, likely on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupee had revisited the near 2-month low of 60.55 per dollar earlier in the session, and retreated after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the greenback via state-run banks starting around 60.53 rupee levels, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the rupee's falls in the past few sessions.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  assured markets that India is watching the situation in Iraq, but despite the uncertainty the domestic economy is better prepared to deal with any shocks on the external front.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude rose towards $114 a barrel on Wednesday as Sunni militants pushed forward in northern Iraq, striking a key refinery near Baghdad and stoking worries about oil exports from the key producer.\par \par \uc2 India imports nearly two-thirds of its oil needs, leaving its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  especially vulnerable to price swings.\par \par \uc2 A fall in domestic stocks due to waning risk appetite added to the rupee's losses.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares fell over 1 percent on Wednesday as oil refiners such as \uc2 Bharat Petroleum Corp\uc2  slumped on concerns about the impact of higher oil prices on inflation and the government's finances.\par \par \uc2 The dollar also notched up broader gains against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the outcome of the U.S. Federal Reserve's two-day meet later in the day.\par \par \uc2 The greenback's strength offset the impact from exporter dollar sales in the domestic market.\par \par \uc2 The dollar held its gains on Wednesday after a broad firming on the back of higher-than-expected U.S. consumer prices for May that fanned speculation the \uc2 Fed\uc2  may inch closer towards hiking interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "I don't see any surprise from \uc2 Fed\uc2 , and the rupee move will depend on crude prices. Any sharp move will be countered by the RBI," said Uday Bhatt, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with \uc2 UCO Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 60.39/40 per dollar versus its previous close of 60.03/04.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, Reuters reported the \uc2 Indian government\uc2  expects oil prices to rise as high as $120 per barrel for several months due to the conflict in Iraq, potentially driving a hole of at least 200 billion rupees ($3.3 billion) in the budget, two government sources said.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 60.70, while the three-month was at 61.29. FACTORS TO WATCH * Dlr supported before \uc2 Fed\uc2 , sterling retreats after BoE minutes * Stocks hit 12-day lows; \uc2 Fed\uc2 , Argentina in focus * Dlr holds firm as mkts sniff risks of \uc2 Fed\uc2  hawkishness * Foreign institutional investor flows INFII INFII01 * For data on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures INRFUTURES DIARIES & DATA: Indian Data Watch ECONIN European diary WEU/EQTY2 Indian diary IN/DIARY US Diary US/DIARY (Editing by Sunil Nair) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-18T12:42:04.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140618ea6i007fx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
