\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee edges down on cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  despite record shares\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2014\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends at 59.20/21 per dlr vs 59.17/18 on Fri\par \par \uc2 * RBI seen buying dlrs throughout the day in small amts\par \par \uc2 * Traders expect INR to hold in 58.80-59.40 range this week\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 June 9 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee weakened on Monday as continued dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and demand for the greenback from importers offset positive sentiment due to record high domestic shares.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares surged on Monday to record highs as blue chips continued to rally on hopes of wide-ranging reforms by the new Narendra Modi government.\par \par \uc2 Inflation will remain a top priority for the government, President Pranab Mukherjee told parliament while finance minister Arun Jaitley said economic growth cannot be compromised at any cost while containing inflation and concentrating on fiscal consolidation.\par \par \uc2 Foreign fund flows into domestic shares and debt will remain key for the rupee in the near-term, although traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to step in to buy dollars and prevent any excessive appreciation.\par \par \uc2 "There is good buying seen from state-run banks. The rupee will continue to trade in a tight range," said Vikas Babu Chittiprolu, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with the state-run \uc2 Andhra Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the rupee to remain in a broad 58.80 to 59.40 range over this week.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed at 59.20/21 per dollar compared with 59.17/18 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the rupee rose as high as 58.98, which triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The consumer price inflation data due on Thursday will also be watched, though a large impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is unlikely, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 59.40 while the three-month was at 59.94.\par \par \uc2 FACTORS TO WATCH * Euro hurt by widening interest rate differentials * Global economic recovery signs boost Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  * Asia stocks scale near 3-yr high on U.S. optimism * Foreign institutional investor flows * For data on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures\par \par \uc2 DIARIES & DATA: Indian Data Watch European diary Indian diary US Diary (Editing by Anupama Dwivedi) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-9T12:59:19.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140609ea690078m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
