\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee ends stronger tracking shares; RBI checks rise\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2014\par 13:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends up at 59.17/18 versus 59.33/34 on Thursday\par \par \uc2 * RBI should hold INR in a tight range - trader\par \par \uc2 * FIIs continue to buy for a fifth straight session\par \par \uc2 By Neha Dasgupta\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 6 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose on Friday, tracking a rally in domestic shares to record highs, but broader gains were capped as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollars intermittently through the session to cap gains.\par \par \uc2 Overseas investors bought Indian shares worth a net 13.69 billion rupees ($230.8 million) on Thursday, provisional exchange data showed, buying for a fifth straight day and bringing their total purchases to $8.3 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keeping a lid on rupee gains, sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down 0.1 percent for the week, its second consecutive weekly loss against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The rupee should be held by RBI in a tight range. Ideally it should have been much stronger than it is," said Ashtosh Raina, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed higher at 59.17/18 per dollar versus 59.33/34 per dollar on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's dollar purchases in the spot market and the corresponding paying in the forwards to offset the impact on liquidity have been pushing up the forward premiums.\par \par \uc2 The one-year premium closed at 501.25 points, after hitting 504.25 points during the session, not far from a near two-month high of 506.25 points hit on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee benefited as India's main two indexes surged more than 1 percent to mark record highs on continued optimism about policy reforms by the new government.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 59.30 while the three-month was at 59.86.\par \par \uc2 FACTORS TO WATCH * Euro holds strong after ECB moves, U.S. data dominates * Emerging Europe \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  near post-ECB highs, U.S. jobs in focus * Asia up, Europe more cautious as payrolls loom * Foreign institutional investor flows * For data on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures\par \par \uc2 DIARIES & DATA: Indian Data Watch European diary Indian diary US Diary (Editing by Anupama Dwivedi) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-6T12:49:23.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140606ea66008lb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
