\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Indian rupee rally mostly over; yuan to recover over time\b0\par\par\uc2 757 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2014\par 09:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * For poll data click on\par \par \uc2 * Indian rupee not likely to strengthen further over next 12 months\par \par \uc2 * Optimism around new government, narrowing current account deficit to limit falls\par \par \uc2 * Weak economic, \uc2 Fed\uc2  taper, RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen hindering rupee appreciation\par \par \uc2 * Chinese yuan to recover slowly, rise to 6.07 in a year\par \par \uc2 By Sumanta Dey\par \par \uc2 BANGALORE, June 6 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee will only make scant gains in the next 12 months as the economy remains weak, although optimism around a new government and a narrowing current account deficit will underpin the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Reuters poll found.\par \par \uc2 The rupee is among the best-performing emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, rising 4 four percent since January.\par \par \uc2 It hit a one-year high of 58.25 against the dollar on May 22 - a week after Prime Minister Narendra Modi's landslide victory in general elections.\par \par \uc2 But analysts believe its rally is largely over.\par \par \uc2 The poll of over 30 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists, conducted June 2-5, predicted one U.S. dollar will fetch 59.25 rupees by the end of June, 59.20 in three months and 60.16 in a year. It was trading around 59.10 early on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Still, those are the strongest rupee forecasts in a long while. The consensus rose above 60 per dollar in the one- and three- month horizons for the first time since August and follow strong net inflows into Indian financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Over 337 billon rupees in foreign money poured into Indian stocks and bonds last month, up from almost nothing in April. India's stock market is trading near a record high.\par \par \uc2 "Much of the rupee's gains in May (were) driven by post-election optimism via portfolio flows into both equities and \uc2 Indian government\uc2  bonds," wrote Derek Halpenny at BTMU, who is expecting the rupee to trade at 59 per dollar in a year.\par \par \uc2 "Modi has been sending all the right signals so far, with considerations to allow at least 49 percent of foreign investments into all sectors."\par \par \uc2 The ruling Bharatiya Janata Party, the first to win a majority in three decades, is expected to quickly pass key economic reforms and raise foreign investment caps in various sectors of the economy, including defence companies.\par \par \uc2 The first peek into the new government's policies will come around early July when Finance Minister Arun Jaitley unveils his maiden budget.\par \par \uc2 Recent data showing a sharp narrowing in the current account deficit to just 0.2 percent of gross domestic product should also prop up the rupee in the interim.\par \par \uc2 Still, weak growth will probably prevent the rupee from any significant break higher. The economy grew just 4.6 percent in the Jan-March quarter.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve's current track to end its economic stimulus before year-end will also hold it back. And the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market daily, buying dollars to prevent sharp rises in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strong foreign inflows.\par \par \uc2 YUAN\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan is expected to slowly recover from a sharp slide earlier this year. That correction was believed to be engineered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only go one way - up.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has been the worst performing emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia so far this year, losing 3 percent against the dollar, which wiped out all of its gains seen in 2013.\par \par \uc2 But it has shown some signs of stabilising in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The yuan is expected to trade at 6.24 per U.S. dollar by the end of June, appreciating to 6.19 in three months and further to 6.07 by May 2015. It was at 6.25 on Friday morning.\par \par \uc2 Beijing has announced a series of modest stimulus measures in recent months after the economy got off to a weak start this year. Business surveys in the last week signal activity may be starting to stabilise but a slight pick-up in parts of the economy does not mean a solid, broader recovery is under way.\par \par \uc2 Short positions on the yuan are now at their smallest level since late February, a separate Reuters poll showed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 That poll also showed long positions on the rupee fell by around a third in the last two weeks amid persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the poll see )\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 59.245 rupees) (Additional reporting and analysis by Shaloo Shrivastava; Editing by Ross Finley & Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-6T08:00:00.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140606ea66004q1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
