\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee snaps three-day fall on good dollar inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2014\par 13:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends at 58.93/94 per dlr vs 59.04/05 on Tues               \par \par \uc2 * Good dlr inflows from corporates, foreign funds seen               \par \par \uc2 * INR seen in 58.50 to 59.50 range in rest of the week               \par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat               \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee snapped a three-day losing streak on Wednesday as dollar inflows related to foreign funds and companies helped offset heavy month-end demand for the greenback from oil and other importers.               \par \par \uc2 Traders also cited occasional dollar buying by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not believed to be as aggressive as in recent weeks.               \par \par \uc2 Traders will continue to focus on the measures new Prime Minister Narendra Modi led government will take to bring down the fiscal deficit and fight inflation.               \par \par \uc2 "There was good dollar selling seen today, likely some corporate flows as well. Foreign banks were mostly on the sell side while there were importers and state-run firms seen bidding," said A. AjithKumar, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with \uc2 Federal Bank\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "There is a good technical support for the pair at 58.35 levels which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defended last time. If that level is broken we could see the pair fall more, if not, we could head back towards 59.50 again," he added.               \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed at 58.93/94 per dollar compared to 59.04/05 on Tuesday.               \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have bought a net $1.46 billion in debt over the past four sessions, bringing their total buying so far this month to $3 billion. In shares, despite some modest selling over the past few sessions, net inflows in May are $2.4 billion.               \par \par \uc2 In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 59.21 while the three-month was at 59.76.                              \par \par \uc2 FACTORS TO WATCH * Euro heads back towards 3-month lows, yuan slides       * U.S. data, weak yuan drag on Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sing dlr up   * Asia stx scale 1-yr highs on brightening U.S. view  * Foreign institutional investor flows          * For data on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-28T12:39:42.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140528ea5s00dcn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
