\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Mostly Lower; Thailand Baht Weak -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2014\par 02:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2200-6.2435   6.2000-6.2500 \par USD/TWD   30.130-30.180   30.000-30.230 \par USD/KRW    1,026-1,030     1,022-1,032 \par USD/SGD   1.2500-1.2523   1.2494-1.2555 \par USD/MYR   3.2180-3.2335    3.2000-3.2450 \par USD/THB    32.50-32.54     32.38-32.62 \par USD/PHP    43.53-43.80     44.50-43.90 \par USD/IDR   11,420-11,470   11,360-11,500 \par USD/INR    59.17-59.68     59.00-60.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. As benchmark \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bond yields continue to slump the dollar will likely struggle against the yuan unless the PBOC steps in to artificially depress the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. The daily USD/CNY benchmark rate is likely to slide toward 6.1600 from Thursday's 6.1640 to reflect weakness in the U.S. dollar index. Activity in the spot USD/CNY market has dwindled as traders steer away from betting on the yuan while the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains a heavy hand on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The main theme for the yuan in the near-term remains the possibility of continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the PBOC to introduce more two-way volatility for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2200 (psychological support), before 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 6.2435 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 6.2500 (psychological resistance), before 6.2807 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downside bias. USD/TWD is likely to drift lower within the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that caps at 30.180--though the move may be slow owing to the gradual downward trajectory of the channel. The U.S. dollar index remains under pressure--owing to declining \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields which make it less attractive to hold the dollar--and is likely to weigh on USD/Asia in general. The pricing of the most-commonly traded one-month nondeliverable forward contract in the offshore market suggests a neutral stance towards the Taiwan dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.130 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.180 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.230 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.280 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW has lost its bearish technical bias after having exited the Bollinger downtrend channel on Wednesday and may now consolidate within a technical range of 1,026-1,032. Despite the weakness of the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield which sank the dollar broadly overnight, USD/KRW is likely to be supported on dips as traders expect \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  to step in again if the won heads for 1,020-1,022. Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  on Wednesday around that level triggered a jump in USD/KRW to as high as 1,030. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,026 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,022 (suspected BOK \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level), before 1,020 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,030 (round-figure trading barrier ), before 1,032 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD is still stuck in a technical consolidation zone but there is a strong likelihood that the U.S. unit will slide toward the lower end of its current 1.2494-1.2523 range owing to the depressed U.S. 10-year Treasury yield. On the weekly chart USD/SGD is beneath the Ichimoku Cloud support zone and also within the Bollinger downtrend channel suggesting more weakness ahead for the U.S. unit. Traders are paying more attention to the recent drop in \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields now that the benchmark 10-year bond's yield has slipped below 2.50%. With a lower yield the U.S. dollar is a less attractive asset to hold and investors will diversify into other higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.2494 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2450 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2523 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1.2528 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud and top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2555 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--downside bias. USD/MYR has a bearish bias on the daily chart owing to the Bollinger downtrend channel capping the dollar at 3.2335. The downwards trajectory could take the U.S. dollar to 3.2000 in the days ahead. Ahead of Malaysia's 1Q Gross Domestic Product data at 1000 GMT, analysts are optimistic for a number better than 4Q's 5.1% growth. A beat on the consensus estimate of 5.4% could fuel the ringgit toward more strength against the U.S. dollar. An upbeat GDP figure would also bolster the case for the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates--which was hinted at last week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2180 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.2000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 3.1880 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2335 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.2450 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.2500 (20-day Bollinger mid and psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. Conflicting forces may keep USD/THB trapped inside the daily Ichimoku Cloud consolidation zone. While the possibility of prolonged political uncertainty has been hurting the baht, the U.S. dollar has its share of troubles. The consistent decline of \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields makes the dollar unattractive to investors, thus weighing on USD/Asia in general. While the political impasse drags on, fresh gun violence at protests in Bangkok--which has resulted in several casualties--is also keeping the baht under pressure. Unless USD/THB climbs back above the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that caps at 32.54 the baht is not as likely to weaken much more. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.50 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.38 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 32.33 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 32.54 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 32.62 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.80 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--downside bias. USD/PHP continues to look bearish on the daily chart guided toward 43.32 where the weekly Ichimoku Cloud support awaits. USD/PHP appears to hold a clear bearish outlook owing to the overnight decline of the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield and positive sentiment for the peso after the S&P credit rating upgrade. The credit rating upgrade followed the \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's anti-inflationary measure of raising its reserve requirement ratio by one percentage point to limit bank lending. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.53 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 43.50 (psychological support), before 43.32 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (psychological resistance), then at 43.90 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. USD/IDR has entered the daily Bollinger downtrend channel--a bearish signal that could threaten the more important technical support at 11,400 which is the base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud. While the U.S. dollar remains pressured by declining \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields the rupiah has been shining owing to optimism for the coalition led by the PDI-P. The market expects a strong win for the coalition--which claimed about half the legislative seats in the April vote--in the presidential elections scheduled for July 9. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,420 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,400 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 11,360 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 11,470 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,530 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. USD/INR bearish technical bias persists despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday which propelled the dollar to 59.45 from around 59.30. The immediate target for the rupee is the base of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 59.17 followed by the round-figure trading barrier at 59.00 which if breached could trigger a steeper slide. Investor confidence has been boosted by exit polls indicating a likely win for the business-friendly BJP party. The official election results will be announced today. Indian stocks and the rupee have been enjoying an election euphoria boost as investors bet on an improvement in business conditions--though some analysts say that those expecting major changes are too optimistic. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 59.17 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 59.14 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 59.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 58.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 59.68 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 60.14 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 15 May 2014 20:50 ET  USD/Asia Mostly Lower; Thailand Baht Weak -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 15, 2014 20:50 ET (00:50 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140516ea5g0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
