\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-India wholesale inflation eases, but monsoon risk may spark higher prices\b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2014\par 14:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * April WPI 5.20 pct y/y vs 5.73 pct in Reuters poll\par \par \uc2 * Food inflation 8.64 pct y/y in April vs 9.90 pct in March\par \par \uc2 * RBI says comfortable with 8 pct fiscal year-end inflation target (Adds comment from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor in 10th paragraph)\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Rajesh Kumar Singh\par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, May 15 (Reuters) - India's wholesale inflation eased in April helped by a moderation in food prices, but the threat of a below-average monsoon in coming months will fan price pressures that will compound challenges for an incoming government.\par \par \uc2 Wholesale prices in April rose a slower-than-expected 5.20 percent, as a nearly 18 percent drop in onion prices since March slowed down food inflation to 8.64 percent from 9.90 percent in March.\par \par \uc2 The data comes days after consumer inflation hit a three-month high of 8.59 percent in April and industrial production posted a second straight contraction in March.\par \par \uc2 India is facing prospects of poor rainfall due to a possible El Nino weather event that affects wind patterns and can trigger both floods and drought. A strong El Nino in India could trigger lower production of summer crops such as rice, sugarcane and oilseeds.\par \par \uc2 "The probability of a consistent improvement in food prices index seems unlikely in the coming months," warned Shakti Satapathy, a fixed income strategist at AK Capital in Mumbai.\par \par \uc2 A new government is set to take over after results of a five-week long general election are declared on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares have surged to a life-time high and the rupee rallied to its strongest in 10 months after exit polls showed opposition challenger Narendra Modi's Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) and its allies winning a majority in the elections.\par \par \uc2 A win for a BJP-led coalition is expected to set the stage for a revival in confidence and investment in Asia's third-largest economy, battling its worst slowdown since the 1980s.\par \par \uc2 While gross domestic product growth has almost halved to less than 5 percent in the past two years, inflation has been averaging nearly 10 percent, way above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort zone.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 aims to bring consumer inflation down to 8 percent by the end of March 2015 and 6 percent by March 2016, and RBI Governor \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  said on Thursday he was "very comfortable" with that target.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS RALLY\par \par \uc2 Persistently weak growth and high inflation are a predicament for the RBI ahead of a policy meeting on June 3.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  considers price stability a necessary condition for sustainable growth and has raised interest rates three times since last September. But further rate increases run the risk of deepening the economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 Dariusz Kowalczyk, an economist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  in Hong Kong, said the WPI readings should boost capital inflows into India's equity and debt markets and shore up the rupee, which hit a near 10-month high of 59.28 on the dollar after the data.\par \par \uc2 "We continue to expect near-term upside for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the Friday night election results, although gains will be limited by RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kowalczyk said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's National Stock Exchange has gained nearly 22 percent since Sept. 13 when Modi was named as the BJP's prime ministerial candidate on hopes he will end a policy logjam in New Delhi and fast-track reforms.\par \par \uc2 An economic revival, however, depends on the new government's success in controlling inflation and reviving capital investments, which probably grew at their slowest pace in 11 years in the fiscal year that ended in March.\par \par \uc2 These two factors have mainly tarnished the economic track-record of outgoing Prime Minister \uc2 Manmohan Singh\uc2 . As a result, some analysts are cautioning financial markets against getting ahead of themselves.\par \par \uc2 "As such, in order to capitalise on the current market momentum and investor confidence, Modi will urgently need to implement far-reaching reforms, a process that could potentially prove to be painful," said Tom Elliott, a senior analyst at financial advisory firm deVere Group in London. (Additional reporting by Manoj Kumar in SHIMLA; Editing by \uc2 Jacqueline Wong\uc2  and Robert Birsel)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-18T12:47:54.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140515ea5f00614\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
