\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  cuts rupee, won gains; profit-taking hits SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 888 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2014\par 07:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * RBI spotted as rupee hits 11-month high - traders\par     * Won up on stock inflows, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 1,026/dlr\par     * Taiwan dollar gains on capital inflows\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, May 15 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee and South\par Korean won rose on Thursday, when most Southeast Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased on profit-taking, but the gains were pared as\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities in the two countries were seen\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The rupee advanced as much as 0.4 percent to 59.45,\par its strongest since July, one day before results for India's\par election were due. Traders said they spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's central\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the rupee hit the session high. \par     The won gained on stock inflows, while South\par Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were spotted buying dollar\par around the won's high of 1,025.8, traders said.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday suffered its largest\par daily loss in nearly three months as traders cited "strong\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ". Some traders estimated the authorities bought $1\par billion-$2 billion in the previous session.\par     "The authorities became more active as the won does not have\par any significant resistance lines until 1,000 if it breaches\par 1,020," said Jeong My-young, Samsung Futures research head in\par Seoul, referring to the won's value against the dollar.\par     The won is also threatening to again break 10 per yen while\par the euro zone explicitly complained about the euro's recent\par strength, Jeong added.\par     For South Korea, the won's strength against the\par yen is worrisome as the country competes with Japan in key\par overseas markets. On Tuesday, the South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strengthened to 9.9766 to the yen, its strongest since Jan. 2. \par The won stood at 10.0736 to the yen on Thursday.\par     Reuters reported that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is preparing\par a package of policy options for its June meeting, including cuts\par in all interest rates and targeted measures for small companies,\par as policymakers have expressed concerns over a strong euro.\par  \par     Still, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities may only slow the won's appreciation, given the\par country's current account surplus and capital inflows, traders\par and analysts said.\par     The won is unlikely to see sharp corrections even when the\par Federal Reserve starts raising interest rates, Samsung's Jeong\par said.\par     "It will take very long to ease dollar supplies unless\par foreigners dump Korean assets. There are various demands for\par Korean assets," Jeong said.\par     Foreigners turned net buyers of the country's stocks and\par bonds in April for the first time in five months and their net\par inflows hit a seven-month-high, according to the local financial\par regulator's data. \par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar rose on inflows from foreign financial\par institutions, while importers' demand for the U.S. dollar\par limited its upside.\par     Investors stayed cautious over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the Taiwan dollar's appreciation as South\par Korea stepped up efforts to stem the won's gains.\par     Some of the island's companies compete with South Korean\par peers in overseas markets.\par     However, Taiwan authorities have not been spotted buying the\par U.S. dollar yet as inflows are not that large, traders said.\par     \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par     The peso fell as investors covered short positions in the\par dollar on growing caution over potential dollar purchases by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     On Wednesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the session high of 43.53 per dollar, the\par peso's strongest level since Nov. 20, a senior Philippine bank\par trader in Manila.\par     Philippine stocks fell 0.3 percent, while five- and\par 10-year government bond yields  slid.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit eased in subdued trading as investors booked\par profits after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday failed to strengthen\par past this year's high of 3.2155 per dollar.\par     Local funds and hedging-related dollar demand also put\par pressure on the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0527 GMT\par   \f28 \b 