                         1,867                      -                  9,718 \par                                                                  117,115                      -                137,060 \par  \par Liabilities \par Borrowings (c)                                                    38,204                      -                 47,336 \par Trade and other payables                                           7,650                      -                  9,249 \par Deferred tax liabilities                                          20,722                      -                 20,108 \par                                                                   66,576                      -                 76,693 \par -------------------------------------------------  ---------------------  ---------------------  --------------------- \par Total assets held for sale and associated \par  liabilities                                                      50,539                      -                 60,367 \par -------------------------------------------------  ---------------------  ---------------------  --------------------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Due to the status of sale negotiations for the sale of G2 the Board reclassified the Group's interest in G2, including its associated liabilities, as held for sale under IFRS 5 Non-current Assets Held for Sale and Discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from 31 March 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The G2 property, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Infospace\f28 \uc2 \f2 , is located at Dundahera in the Gurgaon district near Delhi. The investment property held for sale is stated at its fair value per the Knight Frank valuation on 30 September 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 G2 was classified as held for sale from 31 March 2013 due to the property being actively marketed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jones Lang LaSalle\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the current interim financial period G2 made a cash distribution of GBP 4.67 million to its Mauritian parent company Gladiolys Realty Inc.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    a)         G2 - Investment property \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The investment property held by G2 was valued at fair value in accordance with the RICS Appraisal and Valuation standards ('The Red Book') by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Knight Frank (India) Private Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  at 30 September 2013, 30 September 2012 and 31 March 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unlike the Company's other projects which are joint ventures between subsidiaries of the Company on the one hand and of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unitech Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  ("Unitech") on the other, in the case of G2 there is a third party involved, Gurgaon InfoSpace Limited ("GIL") which owned the land when the project was conceived in 2004 before UCP's IPO.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The effect of the 2004 agreement is that GIL contribute the land at no cost and receive 28% of the income, while UCP and Unitech together carry out the construction and receive the other 72% of income. [ 23-12-13 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Knight Frank Valuation and all previous valuations are on the basis that the three interests are sold together, and of that total price, 28% is received by GIL, and the other 72% is shared 60% to UCP and 40% to Unitech. While we see from the level and strength of interest from prospective purchasers of G2 that they are apparently prepared to proceed at a level in excess of the total Knight Frank Valuation for 100%, it should be noted that, in the event only the interests of this Company and Unitech are sold, as may be the case thus giving the purchaser a 72% interest in future income, that interest is likely to be valued at a discount compared to the value attributed to 100%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the purpose of this Half-Yearly Report we have continued to treat G2 as an asset held for sale, and valued UCP's interest at 60% of 72% of the Knight Frank Valuation for the full 100% as before, in the light of the ongoing negotiations, and the underlying conservative approach taken by Knight Frank.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    b)         G2 - Corporate deposits \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 G2 has placed three corporate deposits with \f28 \uc2 \f2 SREI Infrastructure Finance Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The deposits, which each have a term of 364 days, earn interest at the fixed rate of 10.9% and may be recalled at any time during their term subject to the giving of ninety days' notice. G2 has also placed three corporate deposits with Aten Capital Pvt Limited. The deposits have terms of 364 days, earn interest at a rate of 16% and can be recalled at any time as they are not subject to a notice period. G2 placed one corporate deposit with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Religare Securities Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The deposit has a term of 364 days, it earns interest at a rate of 11.5% and may be recalled at any time during the term subject to giving thirty days' notice. All deposits are placed with companies incorporated in India.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    c)         G2 - Borrowings \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 G2 has taken borrowings from a financial institution of INR 6.44 billion (31 March 2013: INR 6.51 billion) which are secured by a first charge on its immovable property and receivables. The Company's share of these borrowing is GBP38.20 million at 30 September 2013 (31 March 2013: GBP47.33 million). The loan is subject to interest at 13.75% pa (31 March 2013: 13.25%) and is repayable in monthly installments being fully repayable by 2024.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    10.     Related party transactions \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Parties are considered to be related if one party has the ability to control the other party or exercise significant influence over the other party in making financial or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decisions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As at 30 September 2013 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Lake\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a Director of the Company was beneficially interested in 42,500 Ordinary Shares in the Company (31 March 2013: 42,500).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nectrus Limited, the Investment Manager to the Company, is an affiliate of the Unitech Group, the Company's co-investor in the investment property under construction. It receives a management fee and performance fee from the Company. At 30 September 2013 the amount of management fees due to Nectrus Limited from the Company amounted to GBP1.17 million (At 31 March 2013: GBPNil). At 30 September 2013 Nectrus Limited was beneficially interested in 49,042,428 Ordinary Shares in the Company (31 March 2013: 43,007,428).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unitech Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Company's co-investor, acts as Property Manager for the investment property under construction and receives a fee of 5% of the total cost of construction of each project (exclusive of service tax). The fees payable to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unitech Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  for the half year ended 30 September 2013 totaled GBP0.47 million (year ended 31 March 2013: GBP1.86 million) and the amount outstanding as at 30 September 2013 was GBP0.13 million (31 March 2013: GBP0.56 million).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unitech Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  has provided corporate guarantees to Unitech Hi-Tech Structures Limited, Unitech Developers and Projects Limited and Seaview Developers Limited in respect of their bank borrowings and receives a fee of 1.25% pa of the sanctioned amount from each of those companies. The total fee payable to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unitech Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  for the half year ended 30 September 2013 amounted to INR 42.50 million (year ended 31 March 2013: INR 89.43 million).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unitech Infra Limited, a 100% subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unitech Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  received payments amounting to GBP0.46 million during the half year (GBP0.72 million for the year ended 31 March 2013) in respect of property maintenance and running costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unitech Property Management Pvt. Ltd ("UPMP"), which is a wholly owned subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unitech Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , is rendering its services in respect of management and co-ordination of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and maintenance services of the complexes including the common areas and certain other services. The fees payable to UPMP for the half year ended 30 September 2013 totaled GBP0.84 million (year ended 31 March 2013: GBP1.31 million) and the amount outstanding as at 30 September 2013 was GBP0.18 million (31 March 2013: GBP9,000).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bengal Unitech Universal Infrastructure Property Limited, which is a wholly owned subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unitech Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , received lease rental income amounting to GBP10,000 for the interim period (year ended 31 March 2013: GBP21,000) from Unitech Hi-Tech Structures Limited, with GBP14,000 payable at 30 September 2013 (31 March 2013: GBP6,000).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unitech Hospitality Limited, which is a wholly owned subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unitech Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , provided management services for the food courts located in several of the properties. For this service they received management fees of GBP89,000 for the half year ended 30 September 2013 (year ended 31 March 2013: GBP57,000) of which GBP86,000 remained payable at 30 September 2013 (31 March 2013: GBP26,000).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    11.     Commitments \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group's share of capital commitments in respect of capital expenditure contracted for by the joint ventures as at 30 September 2013 was GBP34.49 million (31 March 2013: GBP52.93 million).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    12.     Subsequent events \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company has been re-registered under the Isle of Man Companies Act 2006 on 2 October 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The company news service from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock