\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Supported; U.S. Data in Focus -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2013\par 01:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0903-6.1000   6.0802-6.1041 \par USD/TWD   29.570-29.680   29.500-29.710 \par USD/KRW    1,058-1,060     1,053-1,063 \par USD/SGD   1.2488-1.2517   1.2452-1.2568 \par USD/MYR   3.2050-3.2260   3.2000-3.2370 \par USD/THB    31.67-31.80     31.52-32.00 \par USD/PHP    43.80-43.89     43.63-43.90 \par USD/IDR   11,600-11,725   11,570-11,800 \par USD/INR    62.50-62.82     62.14-63.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The charts suggest likely consolidation for USD/CNY as it hovers just above the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 6.0903. Overnight rises in the euro balanced by a buoyant USD/JPY could mean that the PBOC will keep the dollar's benchmark rate stable from Friday's 6.1380. The market is looking for the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to set the yuan benchmark exchange rate stronger at year-end, as it typically does, and this view is gaining popularity in the NDF market with more speculators betting on a low USD/CNY fixing in a month to come. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0903 (entrance of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.0900 (psychological support), before 6.0802 (record low). Immediate resistance is at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), before 6.1041 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation higher. USD/TWD is likely to grind higher, as the chart suggests a mild bullish bias toward the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 29.710. The dollar, though softer against the euro, is firm against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and this could support USD/TWD for now. The NDF market is displaying a neutral tone towards the greenback, as the benchmark 1-month NDF discount trades around historically average levels. Taiwan releases its October industrial output data at 0800 GMT. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.570 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.500 (psychological support and base of Ichimoku Cloud), before 29.460 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.680 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. The dollar slips to the Bollinger downtrend channel at 1,058 where it will likely be supported for now. USD/KRW may range within a band of 1,058-1,063 as conflicting signals balance traders' views on the won. The Kospi is up 1.2% thus far but overall dollar strength in Asia may hamper further gains for the won. If USD/KRW ends Monday below 1,058, the dollar may gain downside momentum toward the psychological barrier at 1,050. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,058 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,053 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,060 (psychological resistance), then at 1,063 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 1,067 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. USD/SGD is currently well-supported at around 1.2488 where the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel meets the Ichimoku Cloud support. The coincidence of these two technical support levels makes it less likely to see USD weakness in the near term. The greenback could hence inch higher toward the top of the channel at 1.2517 and possibly to the top of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 1.2568. U.S economic data due this week, including consumer confidence and home prices, could be the next catalyst for a bigger move in the USD/SGD. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2488 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and base of Ichimoku Cloud), then at 1.2452 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2420 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2517 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2568 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR is trending higher within the Bollinger uptrend channel, targeting 3.2260 and possibly 3.2370. The uptrend channel places an interim base for the dollar at 3.2050. Mildly positive news for the ringgit last week, when ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  upgraded its outlook for Malaysia's current A3 credit rating, has become less relevant now as the market returns to betting on a possible U.S. Federal Reserve reduction in monetary stimulus in the near future. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2050 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2000 (psychological barrier), before 3.1980 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is at 3.2260 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2370 (top of Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside bias. With the mass anti-government protest in Bangkok, investor confidence could get further shaken, which may lead to weakness for the baht. The USD/THB chart suggests the dollar is likely to be well-supported by the Ichimoku Cloud at 31.67 and could rally toward the psychological barrier at 32.00 soon. Of late, speculative traders have been shorting the Thai baht in anticipation of more weakness, due to domestic political concerns and slowing economic growth. The National Economic and Social Development Board last week revised down its full-year growth projection to 3.0% from 3.8%-4.3%. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.67 (Ichimoku Cloud support zone), then at 31.52 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel ), before 31.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 31.80 (psychological resistance), before 32.00 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--bullish signal appearing. Today could be the day that USD/PHP breaks through the top of the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 43.89, which would encourage more dollar upside. The dollar is still looking well-bid against most Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve is still on the path toward reducing monetary stimulus in months to come. Onshore oil importers, who were buying large amounts of the dollar last week, might provide further USD demand this week--which could propel USD/PHP higher and thereby spook the speculative short positions into buying back their dollars as well. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.80 (psychological support), then at 43.63 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 43.47 (base of Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.89 (top of Ichimoku Cloud), then at 43.90 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.00 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR is still on the path higher within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, aiming for the next psychological trading barrier at 11,800. The rupiah, which hit a 4.5-year low of 11,725 against the dollar Thursday and Friday, has been under pressure due to the likelihood of the U.S. Federal Reserve reducing monetary stimulus in months to come. Ratings agency Fitch is also downbeat on the Indonesian economy, lowering its growth forecast for next year's Gross Domestic Product to 5.3% from 5.5% in 2013. Unless U.S. economic data due this week is exceptionally poor, the dollar could keep on rising for now. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,600 (psychological support), then at 11,570 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,725 (4.5-year higher and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation. USD/INR has tentatively lost its bullish bias after it closed Friday below the Bollinger uptrend channel. This could mean the USD/INR consolidates between 62.50-62.82 for now. Underlying demand for the U.S. dollar due to oil importers hedging their oil-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs and expectations for a Fed tapering of quantitative easing will keep USD/INR supported on dips. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently been suspected of capping USD/INR, which could deter traders from being too bullish on the dollar. The RBI was suspected to have been selling dollars in the spot market Thursday and Friday near the 63.00 psychological barrier, possibly aware that stoploss orders above that level could trigger a sudden slide for the rupee. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.50 (psychological support), before 62.14 (20-day Bollinger mid-support and base of Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.82 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.00 (psychological trading barrier), before 63.50 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 24, 2013 19:39 ET (00:39 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131125e9bp0005y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
