\par\par \b \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  May Need to Buffer Rupee -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2013\par 04:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0311 GMT [Dow Jones] The India rupee is likely to weaken again today, after a bullish USD/INR technical signal emerged Thursday when the dollar closed above 62.83--the entrance of the Bollinger uptrend channel. The rupee could soon depreciate to 63.51 against the dollar--the top of the USD/INR uptrend channel--though \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might slow the move, said a trader. If the rupee falls too much too soon, expect the RBI to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling dollars in the spot market--as they were suspected of doing Thursday, near the 63.00 psychological trading barrier. Protecting this barrier yesterday was likely an important move because stoploss orders waiting above could have triggered a sharper slide in the rupee. The dollar has been rallying broadly across Asia after the mildly hawkish tone revealed in the U.S. FOMC minutes. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0304 GMT [Dow Jones] Buoyed by a record close above 16,000 points for the Dow Jones International Average, Australian equities continue to push higher in midafternoon trading. Energy shares are the standout, with the subindex up 1.6%, although mining stocks are also rallying strongly. The benchmark S&P/ASX 200 is up 1% at 5339.9, recovering from losses in the past four days. \uc2 BHP Billiton\uc2  (BHP.AU) is up 0.5% and \uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2  (RIO.AU) up 0.6% after the companies' chairmen separately reassured demand from China is likely to remain strong. \uc2 David Jones (DJS.AU) \uc2 is 2.4% higher after staging its annual shareholders' meeting, at which CEO \uc2 Paul Zahra\uc2  said the retailer is well prepared for the Chistmas trading period. Rival retailer Myer (MYR.AU) is up 2.7%. Steven Daghlian, market analyst at CommSec, notes major banks are stronger Friday despite being in the red for a third straight week. ANZ (ANZ.AU), Commonwealth Bank (CBA.AU), \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2  (NAB.AU) and \uc2 Westpac\uc2  (WBC.AU) are all up between 0.6% and 1%. (robb.stewart@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0236 GMT [Dow Jones] Further upside for the dollar versus the Malaysia ringgit, possibly toward 3.2370, now looks more likely. USD/MYR entered the Bollinger uptrend channel Thursday as the dollar surged broadly in reaction to the hawkish tone from the U.S. FOMC minutes suggesting a reduction in Federal Reserve bond-buying could take place in the coming months. Now the Bollinger uptrend channel supports the greenback at 3.2000, which is a psychological trading barrier and also the base of the Ichimoku Cloud--another technical support--thus making it a very strong base off which the dollar could rally. The short-term target for USD/MYR could be the top of the Ichimoku Cloud at 3.2370, though in the interim, the top of the uptrend channel at 3.2250 may cap the dollar. USD/MYR is now 3.2090. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0230 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude-oil futures are slightly lower in Asian hours Friday but trade within a tight price range as investors weigh positive economic data from the U.S. and the ongoing negotiations between western leaders and Iran. Oil had settled higher in overnight floor trade on fewer U.S. jobless claims and better manufacturing data. "The data reflected better U.S. economic conditions which mean a likely boost in crude oil demand," Phillip Futures says. However, the flurry of positive U.S. economic data has also raised concerns that the Federal Reserve may pullback on stimulus soon, which is bearish for oil. Meanwhile, in Geneva a final deal on Tehran's nuclear program between Iran and western countries continues to face hurdles with Iran demanding that the West recognize its right to enrich uranium. Nymex crude is down 22 cents at $95.22/bbl, Brent crude is down 6 cents at $110.02/bbl. (eric.yep@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0227 GMT [Dow Jones] Shares of Japanese exporters are higher as the dollar trends above Y101 (now at Y101.22). \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2  (7203.TO) is up 1.8% at Y6,390 and \uc2 Daikin Industries\uc2  (6367.TO) is 1.6% higher at Y6,580. "The dollar's further rise would have to be driven by a rise in U.S. interest rates," says Naoki Fujiwara, fund manager at Shinkin Asset Management. "If the differentials between U.S. and Japan's interest rates widen, the dollar will strengthen against the yen. If that becomes a sustained trend, investors will begin factoring in higher earnings into share prices as a weaker yen lifts exporters profits," he says. (yumi.otagaki@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0223 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/TWD is slightly higher, with market participants turning cautious about pushing the pair up further after recent rises, say two local traders. The pair is at 29.578, slightly higher than 29.565 traded before the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, which lifted it to 29.636 at the close of the onshore trading session, traders say. A trader says the pair is likely to stay in a consolidation mode; "buying [in the USD] from foreign investors becomes less active as local stocks are rebounding (the Taiex is 0.3% higher) after recent declines, " the trader adds, and tips the pair to trade in a 29.550-29.600 band for the session. Foreign investors were net sellers of NT$10.03 billion worth of local shares Thursday--their largest single-day net selling in three months. (fanny.liu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0221 GMT [Dow Jones] The rupiah, which fell to a 4.5-year low of 11,725 against the dollar Thursday, may weaken further Friday. Currently at 11,695, USD/IDR is in an uptrend within the Bollinger band channel that has been in play since 11 November. The steep rally in USD/JPY overnight has added to upside momentum in USD/Asia, while the likelihood of the U.S. Federal Reserve reducing monetary stimulus in coming months has been an underlying factor for dollar strength. Adding to the bullish view for USD/IDR is the dimming prospect for the Indonesia economy which has been further hampered by last week's surprise interest rate hike by \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 . Ratings agency Fitch this week lowered its growth forecast for next year's Gross Domestic Product to 5.3% from 5.5% in 2013. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0214 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnamese banks led by \uc2 Vietcombank\uc2  (VCB.VH) are holding their USD/VND rates at 21,075-21,115 Friday, unchanged from Thursday, in an effort to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buy more dollars at low costs, despite low liquidity in the local interbank market, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say. For the week ended Nov. 8, the average daily dollar-dong transaction volume in the interbank market was $443 million, down from $665 million a week earlier, according to data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday. "Local commercial banks are trying to keep their rates little-changed because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to buy as much dollars at low cost as possible," says a dealer with a joint stock commercial bank from Hanoi. Gold shops have raised their rates because dollar supply is thin. Private dealers with gold shops say they expect the exchange rate in the free market to move in a VND21,220-VND21,240 range over the weekend and higher next week. (phammuoi.nguyen@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0209 GMT [Dow Jones] Sharp (6753.TO) is up 8.1% at Y321 after a Nikkei report that the LCD panel maker is set to begin production of small- and mid-size LCD panels at its Kameyama No. 2 factory in order to supply to China's \uc2 ZTE Corp\uc2 . "How to raise and maintain high operating rates at its factories has been a challenge for Sharp," says Naoki Fujiwara, fund manager at Shinkin Asset Management. "Hence, the shares has responded positively to the report," he says. Although Sharps' smaller LCD panels business moved into the black at the operating line in 2Q, after losses through 1Q, efforts to increase the production weighting of smaller LCDs at the Kameyama No. 2 plant appear to be running around one fiscal quarter behind plan, notes Mika Nishimura, analyst at Mitsubishi UFJ \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  Securities.(yumi.otagaki@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0159 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/SGD, which entered the Bollinger uptrend channel Thursday, has stopped in its trek higher upon hitting the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 1.2495. Further strength for the greenback depends on the USD/SGD closing Friday above this mark. Failure to do so could result in a pullback and the Bollinger uptrend channel being threatened. If the USD/SGD closes above 1.2495 today, its next target could be the weekly Bollinger mid resistance line at 1.2572. Data released Thursday showed a stronger-than-forecast rise in Singapore's 3Q Gross Domestic Product, but it had little impact on the Singapore dollar, which still reacts more to external factors such as the U.S. Federal Reserve potentially reducing monetary stimulus in months to come. The USD/SGD is now 1.2493. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0142 GMT [Dow Jones] The South Korea won is slightly stronger Friday but the dollar may later take on a more bullish bias if it ends Friday above KRW1,063 - the 20-day Bollinger mid that now acts as a technical resistance. Another factor which could spur USD/KRW higher is the steep rise of USD/JPY overnight. Yen weakness is typically followed by weakness for the the South Korea won as \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to ensure that the won retains its relative value to the yen - which gives South Korea exporters a competitive advantage. The USD/KRW has been trading with a firm tone ahead of the 1,060 psychological support, but has struggled to rally for now due to exporters selling near 1,063, said a trader. The USD/KRW is now 1,061.8. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 21 Nov 2013 22:12 EDT  \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  May Need to Buffer Rupee -- -2-\par \par \uc2 0139 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Japan Tobacco\uc2  (2914.TO) or JT is down 3.5% at Y3,590 after The Yomiuri Shimbun report that the government has decided against raising tobacco taxes in April when a sales tax hike kicks in. The newspaper says multiple members in the government's Research Commission on the Tax System said tobacco taxes increase in 2014 will be impossible as an increase in tobacco taxes amid a sales tax hike could lead to a decline in smokers, which could drastically reduce tax revenue. "The market appears to be concerned that the government might sell its JT shares to make up for lost tax revenue a result of an abandoned tobacco tax hike. That will deteriorate supply and demand conditions of the JT shares," says Naoki Fujiwara, fund manager at Shinkin Asset Management. (yumi.otagaki@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 21, 2013 22:12 ET (03:12 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131122e9bm0008u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
