\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Momentum Gathers; China Hype Fizzles -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,925 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2013\par 01:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.0950   6.0800-6.1000 \par USD/TWD   29.580-29.620   29.4500-29.710 \par USD/KRW    1,070-1,080     1,068-1,084 \par USD/SGD   1.2460-1.2500   1.2416-1.2558 \par USD/MYR   3.2000-3.2170   3.1880-3.2200 \par USD/THB    31.50-31.67     31.48-31.80 \par USD/PHP    43.61-43.80     43.50-44.00 \par USD/IDR   11,500-11,640   11,410-11,800 \par USD/INR    63.47-63.75     63.00-64.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The yuan could slip a tad Wednesday on the back of a slightly stronger U.S. dollar index, which partially determines the PBOC'S daily yuan parity rate. A Wednesday closing above 6.0950 and thereby out of the Bollinger downtrend channel could negate the bearish bias for the dollar. If the Bollinger downtrend channel remains in play, the yuan could appreciate toward the base of the channel at 6.0800 in days to come. China's Third Plenum provided little fodder for markets to mull on, apart from vague comments to relax investment restrictions. There was hardly any mention of the financial reform that investors had been hoping for. Nonetheless, the medium-term outlook for China is unlikely to be adversely affected by the lack of insight from the Third Plenum. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), before 6.0800 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.0950 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), before 6.1090 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--possible upside bias. USD/TWD could soon take on a more bullish approach, if it manages to close Wednesday above the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance that currently caps at 29.620. The dollar grinded higher overnight as U.S. stocks fell over concern that a end to quantitative easing is near. Investors are coming to terms with the fact that the Federal Reserve's tapering is an eventuality that could happen sooner then expected, and would have an impact on markets even if benchmark interest rates are kept low. The sentiment of mild risk aversion can be seen in the NDF market--which is a largely speculative marketplace--where the 1-month NDF premium has risen to nearly flat; it typically trades at a discount to the spot USD/TWD price when risk appetite is strong. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.580 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 29.500 (psychological support), before 29.450 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.620 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--upside bias. USD/KRW remains elevated though immediate upside may be limited as the pair is above the upper boundary of the Bollinger uptrend channel, suggesting the move may have extended beyond the calculated short-term statistical range. Though this does not mean the dollar cannot rally higher, it does imply that a pullback may be due before further upside can be explored. Expectations of the U.S. Federal Reserve reducing monetary stimulus has been the main driver for dollar strength, while recent massive foreign fund inflows into South Korea assets seem to have abated, thus reducing demand for the won. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,070 (psychological support), then at 1,068 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,067 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,080 (psychological resistance), then at 1,084 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. USD/SGD treks higher within the Bollinger uptrend channel, aiming for the top of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 1.2558. The climb higher may however be slow, due to strong selling at levels just above 1.2500, where many orders have been placed, said a trader. The motive for these sell orders could be profit-taking by short-term speculators. But as long as the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, which supports at 1.2460, remains in play, the greenback will still look bullish in the near term. The inevitability of the Federal Reserve reducing monetary stimulus will likely keep the dollar well-bid on dips. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2460 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2416 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2400 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2500 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2558 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR's rally looks stronger now that it has convincingly closed above the psychological trading barrier at 3.2000. The triggering of stoploss orders late Tuesday sent the dollar to as high as 3.2155, which makes the ringgit 1.2% weaker this week. Bearishness for the ringgit may stem from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  being grouped into the current account deficit bracket together with the Indonesia rupiah and India rupee. These beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may suffer disproportionately in the event of global investors pulling out funds when U.S. quantitative easing is reduced. Countries such as Indonesia have attempted to mitigate outflows by pre-emptively raising interest rates--which also help by venting pressure from surging stock markets. \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stood pat on rates so far but analysts think a rate hike early next year is possible. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2000 (psychological support), then at 3.1880 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1690 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2170 (weekly Bollinger mid resistance), then at 3.2200 (psychological resistance), before 3.2270 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. USD/THB appears to be running out of upwards momentum to break the Ichimoku Cloud ceiling at 31.67--which is also the entrance to the Bollinger uptrend channel thus adding to the strength of this resistance level. Failure to close above the Cloud will limit the dollar's rally. For now, USD/THB could trade in a consolidation pattern within the Cloud's borders of 31.48-31.67. Looking ahead investors will be watching for further clues that the Federal Reserve is leaning toward ending quantitative easing early next year--this could spur the next move higher for the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.50 (psychological support), then at 31.48 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 31.35 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 31.67 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance and daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.80 (psychological resistance), before 32.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--possible upside bias. The peso is still under the weather, down as much as 1.4% as analysts tally the economic cost of the super typhoon that hit the country. The Philippines finance minister has said the typhoon could knock off 1.0% from next year's GDP, though most analysts believe the economy will bounce back in the medium term due to the government's strong surplus. Further depressing the peso is the increasingly bullish view that some investors have on the U.S. dollar, as expectations of an early Federal Reserve tapering of quantitative easing get priced into the greenback. Remittances by overseas workers due to the calamity and also due to the year-end holidays have not been enough to bolster the peso thus far. What may help the peso is the looming technical resistance for USD/PHP where the daily Ichimoku Cloud caps at 43.89. But if this key resistance is breached by day's end, the dollar will likely extend its rally. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.61 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 43.50 (psychological support), before 43.46 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (psychological resistance), then at 43.89 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 44.00 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. The rupiah recovered some losses after \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  hiked the benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points to a 4-year high of 7.5%, but the uptrend bias for USD/IDR remains intact, suggesting future rupiah weakness is still likely. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision Tuesday caught the market off-guard as most banks had expected BI to stay pat on rates after the last two hikes in August and September. This signals that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking a pre-emptive approach to mitigate the fallout from an end to U.S. quantitative easing. Raising the interest rate puts Indonesia ahead of the curve, buffering it from future volatility when U.S. interest rates start to rise as well. The increase in the base lending rate also hit Indonesia equities, which fell 1.4% on Tuesday, but may be a welcome venting of pressure from a possibly inflated stock market. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,500 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,410 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 11,640 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 12 Nov 2013 19:50 EDT  USD/Asia Momentum Gathers; China Hype Fizzles -- -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--possible upside bias. A bullish USD/INR signal may be confirmed Wednesday that could see the rupee extend its losses this week--which already amount to 2.1% as of its Tuesday trough of 63.84 to the dollar. If USD/INR ends the day above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance at 63.75, the dollar is likely to head even higher toward the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 64.56. The fall of the rupee may be cushioned by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though only to a slight extent, said a trader. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market on Friday and Monday, though it failed to stop the rupee weakening subsequently. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 63.47 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and bottom of Ichimoku Cloud), then at 63.00 (psychological support), before 62.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 63.75 (top of Ichimoku Cloud), then at 64.00 (psychological resistance), before 64.56 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones 