\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Firm; Ringgit Rupee Rupiah May Fall -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,798 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2013\par 02:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.0950   6.0815-6.1000 \par USD/TWD   29.500-29.590   29.450-29.620 \par USD/KRW    1,070-1,080     1,068-1,084 \par USD/SGD   1.2450-1.2485   1.2412-1.2500 \par USD/MYR   3.2000-3.2170   3.1820-3.2200 \par USD/THB    31.50-31.67     31.46-31.70 \par USD/PHP    43.50-43.60     43.48-43.80 \par USD/IDR   11,500-11,635   11,490-11,800 \par USD/INR    63.00-63.50     62.80-63.53 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. As markets await the release of details of the Third Plenum--the top-level meeting of Chinese leaders to chart future economic direction--the yuan is likely to hold its ground. Analysts are expecting the meeting to touch on key areas such as further opening up of the capital account, and possibly further liberalization of interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. The U.S. dollar eased slightly overnight as seen in the ICE dollar index, which could mean that the PBOC daily yuan parity rate could be set slightly stronger for the yuan. USD/CNY is still within its daily Bollinger downtrend channel so the technical bias for yuan appreciation is intact. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), before 6.0815 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.0950 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), before 6.1090 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation higher. USD/TWD has breached the psychological barrier at 29.500 and is likely to consolidate within a range of 29.500-29.620, capped by the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are taking a backseat as the greenback remains broadly firm on expectations of a possible tapering of quantitative easing by the Federal Reserve early next year. The technical bias could shift towards more bullishness for USD/TWD on a daily close above 29.710 which would place the pair above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. Evidence of increased USD-short covering has appeared in the offshore NDF market, where the 1-month NDF premium has risen to nearly par, said a trader--it typically trades at a discount to the spot USD/TWD price. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.500 (psychological support), then at 29.450 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 29.350 (entrance of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.590 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 29.620 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--upside bias. USD/KRW remains elevated despite a brief respite in dollar strength against the majors overnight. USD/KRW has spiked slightly past the confines of the Bollinger uptrend channel, suggesting momentum is strong for this rally. The psychological trading barrier at 1,080 could soon be tested as USD-short covering accelerates. But if USD/KRW stays outside of the upper Bollinger band (second standard deviation) for more than a few sessions, a lower technical retracement could then occur. The street appears to be short dollars, said a trader, and speculators are rushing to buy their dollars back upon seeing a lack of exporters selling USD/KRW; the inflows from exporters repatriating their earnings typically pressures USD/KRW lower. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,070 (psychological support), then at 1,068 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,066 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,080 (psychological resistance), then at 1,084 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD's failure to convincingly break the 1.2500 psychological barrier on two consecutive occasions suggests an abundance of sellers lurking above the level, which could deter further upside attempts for now. Thus USD/SGD may consolidate within a range of 1.2450-1.2500, supported by the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. If the base of the uptrend channel is broken, the upside bias for the greenback could be negated. The continuation of the U.S. stock market's record run could filter into Asia equities today and instill confidence in Asia bourses which may translate into support for their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2450 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2412 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2400 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2485 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2500 (psychological resistance), before 1.2558 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR has breached the 3.2000 psychological barrier and could soon head to the weekly Bollinger mid at 3.2170 if stoploss orders kick in. The dollar looks firm against the ringgit Tuesday despite the overnight softening of the dollar index--which measures the greenback's movement against the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ringgit, one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  grouped into the current account deficit bracket together with the rupiah and rupee, may suffer disproportionately in the event of global investors pulling out funds when U.S. quantitative easing is reduced. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2000 (psychological support), then at 3.1820 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1680 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2170 (weekly Bollinger mid resistance), then at 3.2200 (psychological resistance), before 3.2270 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--possible upside bias. USD/THB has hit a peak not seen since mid-September, driven by expectations of the U.S. Federal Reserve reducing stimulus, and also due to political unrest in Thailand. More baht weakness may ensue if USD/THB ends the day above 31.70, which would place the pair above the Ichimoku Cloud and inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. But this seems less likely for now, after the Thai Senate late Monday rejected the bill that would have allowed exiled ex-leader Thaksin to return to the country--the crux of the protests that spread into Bangkok this week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.50 (psychological support), then at 31.46 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 31.36 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 31.67 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 31.70 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.80 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--well-capped. After the steep 0.9% fall of the peso Monday, some reprieve may be in sight for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/PHP is unlikely to rise further in the near-term, as the U.S. dollar index softens a tad overnight and the technical resistance of the daily Ichimoku Cloud looms over at 43.60. The market has turned slightly bearish on the peso after the massive typhoon that hit the country resulted in economic damage that could knock off 1.0% from next year's GDP, said the Philippines finance minister. The inflow of foreign aid money and increased remittances by overseas workers due to the calamity and also due to the year-end holidays could help the peso to recover soon. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.50 (psychological support), then at 43.48 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 43.20 (200-week moving average support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.60 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 43.80 (psychological resistance), before 43.89 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR is likely to rally further, now that the Bollinger uptrend channel has come into play on the daily chart. The technical bullish signal suggests the dollar may soon hit 11,635--the top of the channel--before finding a firm ceiling. The greenback has been rallying on recently upbeat U.S. economic data, which make it more likely for the Federal Reserve to reduce monetary stimulus early next year. The market is expecting \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  to stay pat on the benchmark interest rate at its policy meeting today. However, some analysts are not ruling out another rate hike to tame inflation, even if it could subtract from economic growth. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,500 (psychological support), then at 11,490 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,385 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 11,635 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation higher. The rupee is likely to remain under pressure as the market reacts nervously to the possibility of the U.S. Federal Reserve tapering monetary stimulus early next year. This anxiety was seen in the rupee's 1.6% drop Monday. USD/INR may next test the Ichimoku Cloud resistance at 63.53 before it manages to stabilize. Monday's sharp move could have been exacerbated by the absence of dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some speculative participants may have shorted the dollar in expectation that the RBI would not allow the rupee to weaken; the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market on Friday near the 62.80 level, but was not seen Monday, thus spooking the dollar shorts, said a trader. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 63.00 (psychological support), then at 62.80 (psychological support), before 62.44 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 63.50 (psychological resistance), then at 63.53 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 63.75 (top of Ichimoku Cloud and entrance to Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 11 Nov 2013 20:13 EDT  USD/Asia Firm; Ringgit Rupee Rupiah May Fall -- -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 11, 2013 20:13 ET (01:13 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131112e9bc0004a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
