\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank sold net $3.55 bln in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  spot market in Sept vs $2.46 bln in Aug\b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2013\par 12:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's net sales in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market rose to $3.55 billion in September from $2.46 billion in August, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, indicating higher \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The net outstanding forward dollar sales was at $9.58 billion as of September compared with $9.05 billion in August showing that the RBI retired some of its forward dollar contracts by taking delivery of the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The spot \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which was also partially due to the dollar inflows coming through the concessional swap windows opened for banks late-August, helped the rupee to recover from its record low of 68.85 to the dollar on Aug. 28. The rupee gained 5 percent in September, its biggest monthly gain in a year. (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury, additional reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Anand Basu)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131114e9bb000vm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
