\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Climbs on U.S. Jobs Data, Tapering Bets -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,847 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2013\par 01:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.0960   6.0820-6.1000 \par USD/TWD   29.450-29.500   29.350-29.590 \par USD/KRW    1,065-1,067     1,062-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2442-1.2475   1.2409-1.2500 \par USD/MYR   3.1800-3.1950   3.1660-3.2000 \par USD/THB    31.46-31.50     31.37-31.67 \par USD/PHP    43.20-43.50     43.00-43.60 \par USD/IDR   11,350-11,480   11,300-11,500 \par USD/INR    62.20-62.57     62.00-63.0 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation higher. Strong Chinese data released over the weekend could support the yuan against a broadly stronger USD which rose after better-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls on Friday. The dollar/yuan parity rate might be set higher than Friday's 6.1355 as the dollar index rose sharply against the majors. But spot USD/CNY may hover under the 6.1000 psychological barrier as the market awaits news out of China's Third Plenum - which could reveal steps toward further economic reform. China's October industrial production rose 10.3% on year while inflation ticked up to 3.2% from 3.1%. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), before 6.0820 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.0960 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), before 6.1100 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation higher. USD/TWD could rise to consolidate above the psychological barrier at 29.500 as the greenback rallied broadly again Friday night. The odds for the U.S. Federal to reduce monetary stimulus early next year may have increased after U.S. non-farm payrolls surprised to the upside, adding to evidence that the U.S. economy is recovering well. Earlier last week U.S. 3Q GDP rose sharply. USD/TWD is likely to be propped up by the entrance of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that lies at 29.450 and may be aiming for the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that caps at 29.590. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.450 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.350 (entrance of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 29.260 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.500 (psychological resistance), then at 29.590 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 29.620 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--upside bias. USD/KRW gaps higher to open at 1,067.0 from its Friday close of 1,064.9, implying a weaker won. The dollar jumped late last week after stronger-than-forecast U.S. jobs data. The USD/KRW pair is now in the daily Bollinger uptrend channel and is likely to aim higher toward the psychological resistance at 1,080 in the near-term. The dollar is broadly higher in Asia, despite risk sentiment looking healthy as stocks rally in sync with Wall Street. Expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve to reduce monetary stimulus have been raised now with strong GDP growth and positive job creation statistics. Reducing bond buying would cause \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields to rise, which would further lift the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,065 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,062 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1,060 (psychological support and daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,067 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,070 (psychological resistance), before 1,080 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. Additional upside momentum stemming from a stronger-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls report on Friday may push USD/SGD toward 1.2500 and possibly 1.2558. The bullish technical signal which appeared in USD/SGD last week has been affirmed as the string of upbeat U.S. economic data makes it more likely the Federal Reserve will taper quantitative easing sooner than expected. The immediate effect of the Fed reducing stimulus will propel the greenback higher first before the implication of a stronger global economy will help the Sing dollar to gain. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2442 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2409 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2400 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2475 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2500 (psychological resistance), before 1.2558 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR is likely to bounce off the bottom of the Bollinger uptrend channel and head toward 3.2000 on the positive U.S. jobs report released Friday. The greenback spiked late last week as the data suggests an impending Federal Reserve tapering of monetary stimulus, possibly as soon as December. The ringgit is thus likely to weaken again, despite the optimism in global stock markets brought on by the prospect of a sustained U.S. economic recovery. If the 3.2000 psychological barrier - above which there are likely stoploss orders lurking - is breached, USD/MYR may spike to the weekly Bollinger mid at 3.2170. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.1800 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.1660 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 3.1500 (psychological support and daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.1950 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2000 (psychological trading resistance), before 3.2170 (weekly Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside bias. An upbeat U.S. jobs report released Friday boosts the dollar, while protests that spread to Thailand's capital add to baht woes, sending USD/THB sharply higher. The baht is now at a 1-month low of 31.48 to the dollar, and may weaken further, charts suggest. USD/THB has breached the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and is now propped up by the Cloud base at 31.46, from which the dollar could rally on to the top of the Cloud at 31.67 in days to come. The ongoing protests by the Thai 'Red Shirts' group is creating political instability that could shake investors' confidence in the nation. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.46 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 31.37 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 31.20 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 31.50 (psychological resistance), then at 31.67 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 31.72 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP may open Monday higher in reaction to the overnight jump in the dollar index triggered by strong U.S. payrolls data, but upside may be capped by continued selling of dollars for remittance inflows. Bank analysts are expecting overseas workers' remittances to rise to a new peak this year, which will buffer the peso against the dollar's current rally. More jobs were added in the U.S. last month, soundly beating bearish expectations and reinforcing the view that the Federal Reserve might sooner-than-expected reduce monetary stimulus. The broad rise of the dollar index has weakened most South East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the peso may be immune for now as the million-strong overseas work force sends more money home before the major holiday season. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.20 (200-week moving average support), then at 43.00 (psychological support), before 42.98 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.50 (psychological resistance and 20-day Bollinger mid), before 43.60 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. The stronger dollar remains the key theme in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, after a much-better-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls report on Friday. The likelihood of USD/IDR rising into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel - which begins at 11,480 -has increased after the ICE dollar index broke through technical resistance late last week. The greenback has been rallying on recent improvements in U.S. GDP as well as job creation data, which make it more likely for the Federal Reserve to reduce monetary stimulus early next year. If USD/IDR enters the Bollinger uptrend channel - contingent on a daily close above 11,480 - the rupiah could weaken further in the days ahead, possibly to the top of the USD/IDR uptrend channel at 11,630. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,350 (20-day Bollinger mid and daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 11,200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,480 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,630 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--possible upside bias. A bullish USD/INR technical signal could soon be trigger on a Monday close above 62.58 - the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. The dollar received a boost late Friday on stronger-than-epected U.S. job creation data, which makes it more likely the Federal Reserve could withdraw monetary stimulus early next year. However, the market will be wary of pushing USD/INR very much higher amid talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stall rupee weakness last week. What could help the rupee is if the RBI pledges to maintain the dollar/rupee swap facility for oil importers - which effectively removed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's biggest dollar buyers since August. The India \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said that this facility could be gradually removed as the rupee stabilizes. If the oil importers return to the spot market for their dollar-financing needs, the RBI may not be able to cap USD/INR for long. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.20 (psychological support), then at 62.00 (psychological support), before 61.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.57 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 63.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 10 Nov 2013 19:48 EDT  USD/Asia Climbs on U.S. Jobs Data, Tapering Bets -2-\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 10, 2013 19:48 ET (00:48 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131111e9bb0003a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
