\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Rally Accelerates On ECB Cut, U.S. GDP Data -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,896 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2013\par 01:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.0970   6.0830-6.1000 \par USD/TWD   29.450-29.500   29.350-29.580 \par USD/KRW    1,062-1,065     1,060-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2438-1.2462   1.2406-1.2500 \par USD/MYR   3.1800-3.1935   3.1640-3.2000 \par USD/THB    31.20-31.34     31.02-31.38 \par USD/PHP    43.20-43.50     43.00-43.53 \par USD/IDR   11,320-11,480   11,300-11,500 \par USD/INR    62.20-62.57     62.00-63.0 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation higher. USD/CNY may stabilize at a slightly higher level if the PBOC adjusts the daily dollar/yuan parity rate upwards in reaction to the overnight spike in the dollar index. A surprise rate cut by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stronger-than-expected U.S. 3Q GDP gave the dollar a boost, but the yuan should be able to hold its ground as traders are likely bullish on the yuan ahead of the Third Plenum - a high-level meeting of China's leaders - scheduled for this weekend at which further economic reform could be announced. USD/CNY may rebound slightly to the top of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 6.0970 before stalling. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (pyschological support), before 6.0830 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.0970 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1000 (pyschological resistance), before 6.1100 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation higher. USD/TWD could rise to consolidate above the psychological barrier at 29.500 as the greenback rallied broadly overnight. The odds for the U.S. Federal to reduce monetary stimulus early next year may have increased after 3Q GDP rose sharply, signalling the U.S. economy's recovery is accelerating. USD/TWD is likely to be propped up by the entrance of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that lies at 29.450 but if it ends Friday below this mark, dollar downside may resume next week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.450 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.350 (entrance of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 29.260 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.500 (psychological resistance), then at 29.580 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 29.640 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation higher. USD/KRW gaps higher Friday in sync with the jump in the dollar index overnight. The Bollinger uptrend channel, which begins at 1,065, may cap dollar gains for now; but if the pair ends the day above this mark, more dollar strength can be expected next week. The surprise rate cut by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the better-than-expected U.S. 3Q GDP boosted the dollar. As U.S. economic data improves, the street is increasingly positioning for the Federal Reserve to reduce monetary stimulus early next year. Reducing bond buying would cause \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields to rise, which would further lift the greenback. Additionally, it could have an impact on investor confidence, which will hurt the South Korea stock market and the won. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,062 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1,060 (psychological support and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level), before 1,059 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,065 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,068 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,070 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. A bullish technical signal has appeared in USD/SGD, after the USD index spiked overnight due to the surprise \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cut and the glowing U.S. 3Q GDP data. USD/SGD is now within the Bollinger uptrend channel, which supports at 1.2438 and could lead the pair toward the psychological barrier above at 1.2500. The greenback is gaining favor as investors lean toward a possible early-2014 tapering of U.S. quantitative easing. U.S. non-farm payrolls data due later in the global day could add to this conviction. Although improvement in the U.S. economy is beneficial to trade-dependent Singapore, the immediate effect of the Fed reducing stimulus will propel the greenback higher first before the trickle-down effects help the Sing dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2438 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2406 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2400 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2462 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR enters the Bollinger uptrend channel, suggesting more ringgit weakness to come in days ahead. Overnight, the USD index rocketed higher and then subsided after the surprise \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate cut. Also adding to dollar bullishness was the much-better-than-expected U.S. 3Q GDP which makes it more likely that the Federal Reserve will consider reducing monetary stimulus earlier. The ringgit may soon test the 3.2000 psychological barrier above as investors reduce risk-on positions on fear that a U.S. withdrawal of stimulus will lead to a drop in risk appetite. \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its benchmark overnight policy rate unchanged Thursday, flagging risks to economic growth as tighter government spending and higher inflation cool domestic demand. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.1800 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.1640 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 3.1500 (psychological support and daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.1935 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2000 (psychological trading resistance), before 3.2150 (weekly Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation higher. USD/THB is likely to be boosted by dollar-short covering in response to the overnight spike of the dollar index. A surprise rate cut by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the upbeat U.S. 3Q GDP data gave the greenback a boost across the board. Investors might trim short-dollar positions as the recent improvement in U.S. data will probably make the U.S. Federal Reserve less dovish. U.S. non-farm payrolls due later in the global day, which may add to conviction for an earlier Fed tapering of QE, will be tainted by the partial government shutdown in October. USD/THB may test the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance at 31.38 but is likely to be stalled by the looming Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that begins at 31.46. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.20 (psychological support), then at 31.02 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 31.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 31.34 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.38 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 31.46 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP may open Friday higher in reaction to the overnight jump in the dollar index, but upside may be capped by remittance selling of dollars. Bank analysts are expecting overseas workers' remittances to rise to a new peak this year, which will buffer the peso against the dollar's current rally. U.S. 3Q GDP surprised strongly to the upside overnight, reinforcing the view that the Federal Reserve might have to acknowledge the recovery by reducing monetary stimulus. The dollar also rose against the majors due to the surprise \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate cut, though that had only a limited impact on most Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.20 (200-week moving average support), then at 43.00 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel and psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.50 (psychological resistance), then at 43.53 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. The likelihood of USD/IDR rising into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel has increased after the spike of the USD index overnight. The greenback rallied on the surprise rate cut by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sank EUR/USD, and also on a strong U.S. 3Q GDP print which could make it more palatable to the Federal Reserve to reduce monetary stimulus early next year. If USD/IDR steps into the Bollinger uptrend channel - contingent on a Friday close above 11,480 - the rupiah could weaken further in the days ahead, possibly to the top of the uptrend channel at 11,650. Indonesia's Q3 GDP data printed at 5.6% on-year Wednesday, a tad lower than the 5.7% median forecast of analysts polled by Dow Jones and a slower growth rate than Q2's 5.8%. Some analysts foresee another inflation-capping interest hike by \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  again before the end of the year, which would further damp economic growth. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,320 (20-day Bollinger mid and daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 11,200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,480 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,650 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2013 19:57 EDT  USD/Asia Rally Accelerates On ECB Cut, U.S. GDP -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--upside bias. The rupee could weaken Friday as the market prices in the increased likelihood of the U.S. Federal Reserve reducing monetary stimulus sooner-than-expected. USD/INR rose briefly late Thursday, rising above the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance, but then fell abruptly amid talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The RBI may not be able to stall the dollar's rally any further if U.S. non-farm payrolls data due later in the global day add to conviction that the Fed could taper quantitative easing early next year. What could help the rupee is if the RBI pledges to maintain the dollar/rupee swap facility for oil importers - which effectively removed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's biggest dollar buyers since August. The India \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said that this facility could be gradually removed as the rupee stabilizes. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.20 (psychological support), then at 62.00 (psychological support), before 61.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.57 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 63.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 07, 2013 19:57 ET (00:57 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131108e9b80001t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
