\par\par \b \uc2 India's NSE index surges 2 pct; volatility may persist\b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2013\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * BSE index gains 1.83 pct; NSE ends 2 pct higher     * Rupee sees sharp rebound on suspected heavy RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * IT shares make record highs on business outlook optimism\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  services activity shrinks again in August, weakest\par since 2009\par     By Abhishek Vishnoi\par     MUMBAI, Sept 4 (Reuters) - India's NSE index rose 2 percent\par on Wednesday on value buying in blue chip stocks after a fall of\par nearly 4 percent on Tuesday was seen as overdone, while IT\par shares surged on improving business outlook.\par     Shares also tracked a sharp recovery in the rupee after\par suspected heavy dollar selling by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prevented the\par battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from slipping to a record low. \par     However, analysts say volatility may persist as the country\par faces its worst economic crunch since a balance of payments\par crisis two decades ago amid rising conviction that the Federal\par Reserve will trim its stimulus and Washington is seen moving\par closer to a military strike on Syria.     \par     "It's hard to predict which way the market can go as\par negative newsflow continues to come at even lower levels," said\par Deven Choksey, managing director at K R Choksey Securities.\par     The broader NSE index rose 2 percent, or 106.65\par points, to end at 5,448.10, closing above the psychologically\par important 5,400 level.\par     The benchmark BSE index rose 1.83 percent, or\par 332.89 points, to end at 18,567.55.\par     Among recently beaten down blue chip shares, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance\par Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  gained 2.2 percent while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Motors\par Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  ended 4.9 percent higher.\par     IT shares surged on improving business outlook and rupee\par depreciation, dealers said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Consultancy Services Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  ended 3.4 percent\par higher after earlier making its all-time high at 2,078.80 rupees\par while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Infosys Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  gained 2.6 percent after earlier\par hitting a record high of 3,139.90 rupees\par     Bank shares rose on hopes that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may unwind\par its liquidity tightening measures soon now that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Raghuram Rajan\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,\par a former chief economist at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par (IMF), takes charge of affairs. \par     In a reminder of the uphill task he faces, a report on\par Wednesday showed that activity in India's services sector shrank\par in August for the second straight month for its lowest reading\par in four years. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICICI Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 4.4 percent and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Axis Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  ended 2.4 percent higher.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jet Airways (India) Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  ended 5.7 percent higher as\par India's cabinet approved an accord with the United Arab Emirates\par to nearly quadruple airline seats between the two countries over\par three years. \par     The stock has risen 12.1 percent in three consecutive\par session of gains following \f28 \uc2 \f2 Etihad Airways\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' comments on Sunday\par that it expected its investment in the Indian carrier to be\par cleared by Indian authorities "imminently" \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ipca Laboratories Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares surged 7.6 percent\par after the company said in a statement that U.S. Food and Drug\par administration found its oral solid dosage formulations\par manufacturing facility in Pithampur 'acceptable' \par     However, among decliners, real estate companies fell after\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  said late on Tuesday that housing\par loans from banks to individuals should be closely linked to the\par stages of construction. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 DLF Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 0.6 percent, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indiabulls Real Estate\par Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  ended 0.1 percent lower.\par         \par    For additional stocks on the move double click        \par      \par    FACTORS TO WATCH                                             \par * Dollar index near six-week high on Fed 'taper' prospects \par * Brent holds above $115, Syria tension stokes concern     \par * Syria worries check gains on brighter economic data \par * Foreign institutional investor flows          \par * For closing rates of Indian ADRs                       \par                        \par    ASIA-PACIFIC STOCK MARKETS:                                  \par Pan-Asia........ Japan.......   S.Korea... \par S.E. Asia.......        Hong Kong...  Taiwan.... \par Australia/NZ....        India.......  China..... \par                         \par    OTHER MARKETS:                                               \par Wall Street ....         Gold ....... \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .. \par Eurostocks.....         Oil ........  JP bonds... \par ADR Report .....       LME metals. US bonds.. \par Stocks News US.. Stocks News Europe     \par                        \par    DIARIES & DATA:                                              \par Indian Data Watch   Asia earnings diary \par U.S. earnings diary     European diary       \par Indian diary          Wall Street Week Ahead  \par Eurostocks Week Ahead                                   \par                          \par    TOP NEWS:                                                    \par    For top Asian company news, double click on:       \par    U.S. company news  European c