\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S&P rating warning, Middle East fears heap more pressure on sliding India rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 923 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2013\par 09:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * S&P says higher chance of India downgrade than Indonesia\par \par \uc2 * Rupee weakens, hit further by fears of U.S. strikes on Syria\par \par \uc2 * Analysts call on govt to raise fuel prices, but action seen unlikely\par \par \uc2 * Parliament approves costly food bill   (Updates with S&P warning on India, Russia comments on ballistic "objects")\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat and Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 3 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell below 68 to the dollar to near record lows on Tuesday after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  said there was a more than one-in-three chance of a ratings downgrade for the country and as fears of war in the Middle East roiled global markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later extended its losses on the day to more than 3 percent after Russian news agencies quoted the Defence Ministry as saying radar had detected the launch of two ballistic "objects" towards the eastern Mediterranean.\par \par \uc2 Israel later said it had carried out a joint missile test with the United States in the area, as President Barack Obama pushed lawmakers to back his plan to attack Syria.\par \par \uc2 The S&P warning was largely a repeat of comments made to Reuters in late August, and no missiles were reported to have landed in Syria, but Indian investors were so unnerved that the reports exacerbated a sell-off in the rupee and local stocks.\par \par \uc2 The broader NSE index fell more than 4 percent at one point, adding to the challenges facing policymakers struggling to restore confidence in the economy at a time of deepening uncertainty among global investors.\par \par \uc2 "We have a negative outlook on India. We think the chances of a downgrade in the next one to two years is one out of three," said Kim Eng Tan, an analyst at S&P said at a news briefing in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 S&P is the only of the three major credit agencies to have a "negative" outlook on India's "BBB-minus" sovereign rating, and any downgrade would send the country to "junk," dealing a blow to the ruling coalition ahead of elections due by next year.\par \par \uc2 Tan called the chances of a downgrade on India higher than on Indonesia, another Asian country reeling from waning confidence in its economy, worries about its twin deficits and capital outflows. The rupiah fell to a four-year low on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee traded as low as   at 68.27 per dollar from its close of 66.00/01 on Monday, and not far from the record low of 68.85 hit on Aug. 28, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avert a deeper slide.\par \par \uc2 DOWNGRADING RATINGS\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record high current account deficit and fiscal deficit could blow out even further as crude oil prices rise due to fears of a U.S. military strike on Syria.\par \par \uc2 Economists called on the \uc2 Indian government\uc2  on Tuesday to  increase subsidised fuel prices to help address such concerns, but there are doubts whether Prime Minister \uc2 Manmohan Singh\uc2 's minority government would be ready to take such unpopular steps.\par \par \uc2 Technical charts suggest the rupee could fall further, though offshore traders see it hovering near the record low, with one-month contracts for non-deliverable forwards PNDF trading at 68.87.\par \par \uc2 Traders were cautiously awaiting U.S. jobs data on Friday that could effect expectations about when the Federal Reserve will start tapering its monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of less easy money from the United States has caused a exodus of capital from many emerging markets over the past few months, but India has fared worse than most because of its precarious deficits.\par \par \uc2 Markets are also waiting to see how former \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  economist \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  will handle the rupee once he takes over as governor of the Reserve Bank of India on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's rupee defence has so far rested largely on draining money markets, but it has still tumbled more than 20 percent against the dollar since early May, and higher short term interest rates have raised borrowing costs for struggling corporates, threatening to throw another wrench into the already-slowing economy.\par \par \uc2 India is suffering from a dearth of investment, and steps taken by the government so far have failed to convince investors to put more money into the economy.\par \par \uc2 It has unveiled measures to curb gold imports and announced gradual diesel price hikes, but economists say more are needed.\par \par \uc2 "The government will have to raise (fuel) prices to send a clear signal to investors, because if they do not meet the fiscal deficit target, it will be negative for the economy," said Rupa Rege Nitsure, chief economist at \uc2 Bank of Baroda\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors worry the government is more focused on expensive, populist measures that will make it hard for India to meet its target of bringing the fiscal deficit down to 4.8 percent of gross domestic product this fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 "Rating risks are still on the table as the government's ability to rein in last year's fiscal deficit looks likely to unravel this year," said Radhika Rao, an economist at DBS in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "While a downgrade might not be imminent, the ground is still fluid."   (Additional reporting by Christine Kim in SEOUL; Editing by Rafael Nam and \uc2 Simon Cameron-Moore\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 INDIA-MARKETS/ (UPDATE 2) | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | E | RBN | M | O | OIL | ABX | BNX | FUN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD | PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130906e993000a3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
