\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  Blog:Don't Expect the Big Guns for Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Rescues Just Yet\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2013\par 05:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's MoneyBeat blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/moneybeat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/moneybeat/}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Erin McCarthy\par \par \uc2 Investors shouldn't hold their breath for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  among emerging markets to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The idea started making the rounds in markets earlier Friday when Reuters cited Dipak Dasgupta, a senior economic adviser to the India Finance Ministry, as saying \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was talking to other countries about coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He later clarified to The Wall Street Journal that it was his professional view that the countries should coordinate their actions and that he didn't know if India is actively discussing such efforts with any other country.\par \par \uc2 Also Friday, South African Finance Minister Pravin Gordhan warned that the rand's precipitous drop could exacerbate inflationary pressures, adding "we'll have to watch the situation on a day-by-day basis and see what lessons we can learn from others and what defensive measures we can develop on our own side."\par \par \uc2 Analysts broadly agree that any coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be politically and logistically difficult to execute. After all, a place like Brazil will have little motivation to spend its own money to help curb declines in the Indian rupee, when its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, has hit four-year lows recently. But such market chatter reflects the broader need for a plan for these economies to stabilize local markets.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently introduced a plan to inject at least $60 billion more of dollar liquidity into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through the end of the year, while India has announced a slew of policy measures aimed at stemming the rupee's slide. But investor confidence in these countries has yet to return. The Indian rupee is down about 20% year-to-date, while the real is down about 16% against the dollar, and the rand is down nearly 22%.\par \par \uc2 Dan Dorrow, head of research at Faros Trading in Stamford, Conn., said though coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to happen, it's not a bad idea.\par \par \uc2 "If you can stabilize [emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] together, it does in theory...make sense because contagion is the problem," Mr. Dorrow said. "What we need really is a shift in confidence."\par \par \uc2 He says a more feasible solution could be introducing dollar swap lines among some of these troubled economies. \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it had signed a bilateral swap agreement worth $12 billion with the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , and is exploring similar agreements with other central banks.\par \par \uc2 Through these swap lines, central banks can borrow \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  that can be used as ammunition to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability.\par \par \uc2 But others say emerging markets may be jumping the gun by seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -supportive policy bazookas. Benoit Anne, global head of emerging-market strategy at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 , said coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this stage simply isn't necessary.\par \par \uc2 "This is not a financial crisis to me," he said. "This is a bear market after years of a bull market. It feels painful from a market perspective, but it's not that severe."\par \par \uc2 For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 02-09-13 0310GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130902e99200046\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
